msgstr "triton::PtrToIntOp to arith::IndexCastOp"

msgid "3.2.2.4 other passes"
msgstr "3.2.2.4 Other Passes"

msgid "Pass名称"
msgstr "Pass name"

msgid "功能描述"
msgstr "Functional Description"

msgid "核心转换器"
msgstr "Core Converter"

msgid "转换器描述"
msgstr "Converter description"

msgid "triton-to-annotation"
msgstr "triton-to-annotation"

msgid "处理Ascend NPU特有的编译提示指令 (`tl.compile_hint`)，将其转换为后端的Annotation方言，用于指导后续的硬件特定优化或资源配置。"
msgstr "Process the Ascend NPU-specific compilation hint directive (`tl.compile_hint`), converting it into the backend's Annotation dialect to guide subsequent hardware-specific optimizations or resource allocation."

msgid "TritonAnnotationConversion"
msgstr "TritonAnnotationConversion"

msgid "将 `triton::AnnotationOp` 转换为 `annotation::MarkOp`，实现高级编译提示信息向底层注释标记的传递。"
msgstr "Convert `triton::AnnotationOp` to `annotation::MarkOp`, enabling the transfer of high-level compilation hints to low-level annotation markers."

msgid "triton-to-hfusion"
msgstr "triton-to-hfusion"

msgid "将Triton中的`TTIR`转换为Ascend NPU硬件加速器`HFusion`方言中的对应操作"
msgstr "Translate the corresponding operations in `TTIR` from Triton to the `HFusion` dialect of the Ascend NPU hardware accelerator."

msgid "TritonHistogramToHFusionConversion"
msgstr "TritonHistogramToHFusionConversion"

msgid "将 `triton::HistogramOp` 转换为 `hfusion::HistogramOp`，使能在NPU的专用硬件上高效执行。"
msgstr "Convert `triton::HistogramOp` to `hfusion::HistogramOp` to enable efficient execution on NPU-specific hardware."

msgid "triton-to-hivm"
msgstr "triton-to-hivm"

msgid "处理Triton的块同步操作 (`tl.sync_block_all`, `tl.sync_block_set`, `tl.sync_block_wait`)，将其转换为Ascend NPU的`HIVM`方言中的跨核心同步指令。这些指令用于管理多核流水线中的同步与数据依赖，是流水优化的关键。"
msgstr "Handle Triton's block synchronization operations (`tl.sync_block_all`, `tl.sync_block_set`, `tl.sync_block_wait`), converting them into cross-core synchronization instructions in the `HIVM` dialect of Ascend NPU. These instructions are used to manage synchronization and data dependencies in multi-core pipelines, and are key to pipeline optimization."

msgid "TritonCustomOpToHIVMSyncOpConversion"
msgstr "TritonCustomOpToHIVMSyncOpConversion"

msgid "实现Triton同步指令到HIVM同步指令的转换：<br>• `sync_block_all`：全局块同步<br>• `sync_block_set`：设置同步点<br>• `sync_block_wait`：等待同步点"
msgstr "Implement the conversion of Triton synchronization instructions to HIVM synchronization instructions:<br>• `sync_block_all`: Global block synchronization<br>• `sync_block_set`: Set synchronization point<br>• `sync_block_wait`: Wait for synchronization point"

msgid "triton-to-llvm"
msgstr "triton-to-llvm"

msgid "将Triton中的内联汇编操作 (`tl.inline_assembly`) 转换为LLVM方言的内联汇编，并最终映射为Ascend NPU的CCE硬件固有函数（Intrinsics）"
msgstr "Convert the inline assembly operations in Triton (`tl.inline_assembly`) to inline assembly in the LLVM dialect, and ultimately map them to the CCE hardware intrinsics of the Ascend NPU."

msgid "ElementwiseInlineAsmOpConversion"
msgstr "ElementwiseInlineAsmOpConversion"

msgid "将 `triton::ElementwiseInlineAsmOp` 转换为 `LLVM::InlineAsmOp`"
msgstr "Convert `triton::ElementwiseInlineAsmOp` to `LLVM::InlineAsmOp`."

msgid "3.2.3 SIMT Compiler（Ascend 950）"
msgstr "3.2.3 SIMT Compiler (Ascend 950)"

msgid "昇腾 950 在 SIMD 路径之外增加 SIMT 能力，用于加速**非结构化 / 离散**访存（如间接索引的 load/store）。 开发者通过 `compile_mode` 选择编译路径。"
msgstr "Ascend 950 adds SIMT capability outside the SIMD path to accelerate **unstructured/discrete** memory access (e.g., indirect indexed load/store). Developers select the compilation path via `compile_mode`."

msgid "3.2.3.1 `compile_mode` 说明"
msgstr "3.2.3.1 `compile_mode` Description"

msgid "`compile_mode`"
msgstr "`compile_mode`"

msgid "含义"
msgstr "Meaning"

msgid "编译路径"
msgstr "Compilation path"

msgid "`\"simd\"`"
msgstr "`\"simd\"`"

msgid "纯 SIMD：结构化访存走 DMA；非结构化走标量循环"
msgstr "Pure SIMD: Structured memory access goes through DMA; unstructured memory access goes through scalar loops."

msgid "`Triton IR → Linalg IR → AscendNPU IR`"
msgstr "`Triton IR → Linalg IR → AscendNPU IR`"

msgid "`\"unstructured_in_simt\"`（**默认**）"
msgstr "`\"unstructured_in_simt\"` (**default**)"

msgid "混合：结构化仍走 SIMD；离散访存尽量走 SIMT 模板"
msgstr "Hybrid: structured operations still use SIMD; discrete memory access should follow the SIMT template as much as possible."

msgid "`\"simt_only\"`"
msgstr "`\"simt_only\"`"

msgid "纯 SIMT：直接下发 Triton IR 给NPU IR处理"
msgstr "Pure SIMT: Directly issue Triton IR to NPU IR processing"

msgid "`Triton IR → AscendNPU IR`"
msgstr "`Triton IR → AscendNPU IR`"

msgid "用法示例："
msgstr "Usage example:"

msgid "3.2.3.2 三种模式的编译分流"
msgstr "3.2.3.2 Compilation Distribution for Three Modes"

msgid "阶段"
msgstr "Stage"

msgid "`\"unstructured_in_simt\"`"
msgstr "`\"unstructured_in_simt\"`"

msgid "离散 mask 处理"
msgstr "Discrete mask processing"

msgid "拆成连续/离散边界，用 load + select / store 处理"
msgstr "Split into continuous/discrete boundaries, handle with load + select / store."

msgid "Ascend 950 且张量维数 ≤ 5：标记后交给下游；否则同左"
msgstr "Ascend 950 and tensor dimension ≤ 5: mark and pass to downstream; otherwise, same as left."

msgid "不运行"
msgstr "Not running"

msgid "非结构化访存"
msgstr "Unstructured memory access"

msgid "展开为标量循环"
msgstr "Expand into scalar loop"

msgid "尽量转为 SIMT 间接访存（维数 ≤ 5）；失败则回退标量循环"
msgstr "Convert to SIMT indirect memory access (dimension ≤ 5) whenever possible; fall back to scalar loop on failure."

msgid "TritonToLinalg"
msgstr "TritonToLinalg"

msgid "常规 Linalg IR 降级"
msgstr "Standard Linalg IR Lowering"

msgid "3.2.3.3 混合模式：只对离散访存走 SIMT"
msgstr "3.2.3.3 Mixed Mode: Only Discrete Accesses Use SIMT"

msgid "混合模式**不会**把整个 kernel 切到 SIMT，只对离散 / 非结构化访存点走 SIMT，其余仍走 SIMD："
msgstr "Mixed mode does **not** switch the entire kernel to SIMT; it only uses SIMT for scattered/unstructured memory access points, while the rest still uses SIMD."

msgid "**离散 mask 处理**"
msgstr "**Discrete mask processing**"

msgid "若判定为非连续 mask，且满足 Ascend 950、混合模式、维数 ≤ 5：不改写 IR，只标记「下游走 SIMT」。"
msgstr "If it is determined to be a non-contiguous mask and meets the conditions of Ascend 950, mixed mode, and dimension ≤ 5: do not rewrite the IR, only mark \"downstream goes SIMT\"."

msgid "否则（纯 SIMD 或不满足条件）：将 mask 拆成连续 / 离散部分，用连续边界限定全局内存访问，再通过 select 合并结果。"
msgstr "Otherwise (pure SIMD or conditions not met): split the mask into contiguous/discrete parts, use contiguous boundaries to limit global memory access, and then merge the results via select."

msgid "**非结构化访存处理**"
msgstr "**Unstructured Memory Access Handling**"

msgid "在 Ascend 950 混合模式下，对非结构化访存或已标记的离散访存走 SIMT 快速通道："
msgstr "In Ascend 950 hybrid mode, unstructured memory access or marked discrete memory access goes through the SIMT fast path."

msgid "`load` / `store` → `indirect_load` / `indirect_store`（维数 ≤ 5）"
msgstr "`load` / `store` → `indirect_load` / `indirect_store` (dimension ≤ 5)"

msgid "`atomic` 操作 → `hivm.custom(symbol=\"__builtin_indirect_atomic\")`"
msgstr "`atomic` operation → `hivm.custom(symbol=\"__builtin_indirect_atomic\")`"

msgid "不满足条件则回退为标量循环（与 `\"simd\"` 一致）。"
msgstr "If conditions are not met, fall back to scalar loop (consistent with `\"simd\"`)."

msgid "**TritonToLinalg**"
msgstr "**TritonToLinalg**"

msgid "常规 Linalg IR 降级。"
msgstr "Standard Linalg IR lowering."

msgid "3.2.3.4 纯 SIMT（`simt_only`）"
msgstr "3.2.3.4 Pure SIMT (`simt_only`)"

msgid "`\"simt_only\"` 直接下发 Triton IR 交给 AscendNPU IR 做纯 SIMT 编译。"
msgstr "`\"simt_only\"` directly dispatches Triton IR to AscendNPU IR for pure SIMT compilation."

msgid "3.2.4 Ascend affinitive Operators"
msgstr "3.2.4 Ascend affinitive Operators"

msgid "Operator"
msgstr "Operator"

msgid "tl.custom_op"
msgstr "tl.custom_op"

msgid "Ascend NPU扩展的自定义算子集，用于支持硬件特定的内存访问与数据搬运模式，例如：<br>• `index_select`: 基于索引选择数据<br>• `index_put`: 基于索引放置数据<br>• `gather_out_to_ub`: 将外部数据收集到Unified Buffer (UB)<br>• `scatter_ub_to_out`: 将UB中的数据分散输出<br>• `indirect_load`: 间接地址加载<br>• `indirect_store`: 间接地址存储"
msgstr "Custom operator set extended by Ascend NPU, used to support hardware-specific memory access and data transfer modes, for example:<br>• `index_select`: Select data based on indices<br>• `index_put`: Place data based on indices<br>• `gather_out_to_ub`: Gather external data into Unified Buffer (UB)<br>• `scatter_ub_to_out`: Scatter output data from UB<br>• `indirect_load`: Indirect address load<br>• `indirect_store`: Indirect address store"

msgid "tl.compile_hint"
msgstr "tl.compile_hint"

msgid "向编译器传递硬件特定的编译提示信息，用于指导后端优化策略、资源分配或内核配置。"
msgstr "Pass hardware-specific compilation hints to the compiler to guide backend optimization strategies, resource allocation, or kernel configuration."

msgid "tl.sync_block_wait(`sender, receiver, event_id`)"
msgstr "tl.sync_block_wait(`sender, receiver, event_id`)"

msgid "块同步等待操作。指定接收核 (`receiver`) 等待由发送核 (`sender`) 发出的事件信号 (`event_id`)，用于管理跨核流水线中的数据依赖与执行顺序。"
msgstr "Block synchronization wait operation. Specifies that the receiving core (`receiver`) waits for an event signal (`event_id`) issued by the sending core (`sender`), used to manage data dependencies and execution order in cross-core pipelines."

msgid "tl.sync_block_set(`sender, receiver, event_id`)"
msgstr "tl.sync_block_set(`sender, receiver, event_id`)"

msgid "块同步设置操作。指定发送核 (`sender`) 向接收核 (`receiver`) 发出一个事件信号 (`event_id`)，表明某个执行阶段或数据已准备就绪。"
msgstr "Block synchronization setup operation. Specifies that the sending core (`sender`) sends an event signal (`event_id`) to the receiving core (`receiver`), indicating that a certain execution phase or data is ready."

msgid "tl.sync_block_all(`mode, event_id`)"
msgstr "tl.sync_block_all(`mode, event_id`)"

msgid "全局块同步操作。根据指定的同步模式 (`mode`)，向所有相关的接收核广播一个事件信号 (`event_id`)，用于实现全核同步或特定模式的集体同步。"
msgstr "Global block synchronization operation. According to the specified synchronization mode (`mode`), an event signal (`event_id`) is broadcast to all relevant receiving cores, enabling full-core synchronization or collective synchronization in a specific mode."

msgid "Triton-Ascend autotune 使用指南"
msgstr "Triton-Ascend autotune User Guide"

msgid "文档定位"
msgstr "Document Positioning"

msgid "本文面向已经会写 Triton kernel、也了解社区版 `triton.autotune` 基本概念的用户，重点说明 Triton-Ascend 的推荐用法："
msgstr "This article is intended for users who already know how to write Triton kernels and understand the basic concepts of the community version of `triton.autotune`, focusing on the recommended usage of Triton-Ascend."

msgid "Triton-Ascend 上的推荐 autotune 写法；"
msgstr "Recommended autotune writing style on Triton-Ascend;"

msgid "`configs=[]` 在 Ascend 后端中的含义；"
msgstr "The meaning of `configs=[]` in the Ascend backend."

msgid "自动 Tiling 模式的适用边界，以及何时回到手写 `triton.Config`。"
msgstr "Applicable boundaries of automatic Tiling mode, and when to revert to manually writing `triton.Config`."

msgid "快速上手"
msgstr "Quick Start"

msgid "在 Triton-Ascend 上，推荐保留社区版 `@triton.autotune` 的基本写法；当希望系统自动生成并评估候选配置时，将 `configs` 设为 `[]`："
msgstr "On Triton-Ascend, it is recommended to retain the basic syntax of the community version `@triton.autotune`; when you want the system to automatically generate and evaluate candidate configurations, set `configs` to `[]`."

msgid "这表示："
msgstr "This means:"

msgid "`key` 的语义与社区版保持一致，用于决定哪些输入变化会触发重新选择配置；"
msgstr "The semantics of `key` remain consistent with the community edition, used to determine which input changes will trigger re-selection of the configuration."

msgid "`configs=[]` 在 Triton-Ascend 中表示“由 Ascend backend 自动生成候选配置并完成寻优”，而不是“没有可选配置”。"
msgstr "`configs=[]` in Triton-Ascend means \"automatically generate candidate configurations and complete optimization by the Ascend backend\", rather than \"no available configurations\"."

msgid "1. 先启用 Ascend 对 autotune 的扩展"
msgstr "1. First enable Ascend's extension for autotune"

msgid "只有导入下面这行后，才会进入 Triton-Ascend 的 autotune 扩展路径："
msgstr "Only after importing the following line will the autotune extension path of Triton-Ascend be entered:"

msgid "如果没有这一步，使用的仍然是社区版 `triton.autotune`，`configs=[]` 也不会触发 Ascend 的自动 Tiling 生成。"
msgstr "Without this step, the community version `triton.autotune` is still used, and `configs=[]` will not trigger Ascend's automatic Tiling generation."

msgid "2. `@triton.autotune` 必须直接包在 `@triton.jit` 外层"
msgstr "2. `@triton.autotune` must be directly wrapped around `@triton.jit`."

msgid "必须写成下面这种顺序："
msgstr "Must be written in the following order:"

msgid "`@triton.autotune` 必须直接包在 `@triton.jit` 外层，不能在两者之间插入其他 decorator。否则会导致无法对 kernel DSL 进行解析，从而无法进入 Triton-Ascend 的自动 Tiling 生成与寻优链路。"
msgstr "`@triton.autotune` must be directly wrapped around `@triton.jit`, and no other decorators should be inserted between them. Otherwise, the kernel DSL cannot be parsed, making it impossible to enter the automatic tiling generation and optimization pipeline of Triton-Ascend."

msgid "3. `key` 的含义与社区一致"
msgstr "3. The meaning of `key` is consistent with the community."

msgid "`key` 的本质是 autotune 的 cache key。凡是填入 `key` 的参数，只要取值发生变化，就会触发重新 autotune。"
msgstr "The essence of `key` is the cache key for autotune. Any parameter filled into `key` will trigger re-autotuning if its value changes."

msgid "大多数情况下，`key` 里放的是 `M/N/K`、`seq_len`、`hidden_size` 这类 shape 参数，因为它们往往会显著影响最优 Tiling；但 `key` 并不只限于 shape 参数，只要某个参数变化会影响配置选择，也可以放入 `key`。"
msgstr "In most cases, the `key` contains shape parameters such as `M/N/K`, `seq_len`, and `hidden_size`, as they often significantly affect the optimal Tiling. However, the `key` is not limited to shape parameters; any parameter whose variation influences configuration selection can also be placed in the `key`."

msgid "4. 希望参与自动调优的参数不要被提前固定"
msgstr "4. Parameters intended for automatic tuning should not be fixed in advance."

msgid "如果希望某个 `tl.constexpr` 参与自动 Tiling 生成，需要同时满足下面三点："
msgstr "If you want a `tl.constexpr` to participate in automatic Tiling generation, the following three conditions must be met simultaneously:"

msgid "它本身必须是 Tiling 参数，也就是会影响每个 block（逻辑核）处理的数据规模或 tile 大小的参数；"
msgstr "It must itself be a Tiling parameter, i.e., a parameter that affects the data size or tile size processed by each block (logical core)."

msgid "不要在 launch 时把它显式传值写死；"
msgstr "Do not hardcode its value explicitly when launching."

msgid "不要在 kernel 定义里给它设置默认值。"
msgstr "Do not set a default value for it in the kernel definition."

msgid "例如下面这种写法，`BLOCK_M` 会参与自动调优："
msgstr "For example, in the following code, `BLOCK_M` will participate in auto-tuning:"

msgid "如果你在 launch 时显式传入："
msgstr "If you explicitly pass in during launch:"

msgid "那这个参数就已经被固定，不再属于自动生成范围。"
msgstr "Then this parameter has been fixed and is no longer within the scope of automatic generation."

msgid "同样，如果在 kernel 定义中给某个调优参数提供了默认值，例如："
msgstr "Similarly, if a default value is provided for a tuning parameter in the kernel definition, for example:"

msgid "那么这个参数也不会参与自动调优。对于希望交给框架自动生成和寻优的参数，应该把它保留为“未在 launch 时显式传值、且在 kernel 定义中也没有默认值”的 `tl.constexpr`。"
msgstr "Then this parameter will not participate in automatic tuning. For parameters that are intended to be automatically generated and optimized by the framework, they should be kept as `tl.constexpr` that are \"not explicitly passed a value at launch time and have no default value in the kernel definition.\""

msgid "5. 如果 Tiling 参数会影响 grid，grid 必须写成 lambda 形式"
msgstr "5. If the Tiling parameter affects the grid, the grid must be written in lambda form."

msgid "如果某个 Tiling 参数会影响 grid 大小，那么 grid 不能提前写成固定值或只依赖运行时参数的静态表达式，而必须写成依赖 meta 参数的 `lambda` 形式。这一点与社区 autotune 的要求一致。"
msgstr "If a Tiling parameter affects the grid size, the grid cannot be written as a fixed value or a static expression that only depends on runtime parameters. Instead, it must be written as a `lambda` form that depends on meta parameters. This is consistent with the requirements of the community autotune."

msgid "原因是 autotune 在评估不同候选配置时，`BLOCK_M` 这类参数的取值会变化；如果 grid 不随候选配置一起变化，就无法保证每个候选配置都以正确的发射方式执行。"
msgstr "The reason is that when autotune evaluates different candidate configurations, the values of parameters such as `BLOCK_M` will change; if the grid does not change along with the candidate configuration, it cannot be guaranteed that each candidate configuration is executed with the correct launch method."

msgid "使用注意事项"
msgstr "Usage Precautions"

msgid "autotune 的 benchmark 语义与社区一致，会多次执行 kernel。如果 kernel 存在副作用，例如包含原子操作、inplace 写入，或会修改输入/输出 buffer 的累积状态，仍然需要通过社区已有的 hook 机制处理。"
msgstr "The benchmark semantics of autotune are consistent with the community, executing the kernel multiple times. If the kernel has side effects, such as containing atomic operations, inplace writes, or modifying the cumulative state of input/output buffers, it still needs to be handled through the existing hook mechanism in the community."

msgid "Triton-Ascend 相比社区 autotune 的扩展"
msgstr "Triton-Ascend's extension compared to the community autotune"

msgid "社区版 `triton.autotune` 的典型模式是：用户手工提供一组 `triton.Config`，框架做 benchmark，然后缓存最优结果。"
msgstr "The typical pattern of the community edition `triton.autotune` is: users manually provide a set of `triton.Config`, the framework performs benchmarking, and then caches the optimal result."

msgid "Triton-Ascend 在保持这套接口习惯不变的前提下，主要扩展了下面几件事。"
msgstr "Triton-Ascend primarily extends the following aspects while keeping the interface conventions unchanged."

msgid "1. 支持 `configs=[]` 自动生成候选配置"
msgstr "Supports `configs=[]` to automatically generate candidate configurations."

msgid "这是最核心的扩展。用户不必先手写一组 `triton.Config`，而是可以把 `configs` 留空，让 Ascend backend 根据 kernel DSL 语义和运行时 shape 自动生成候选配置。"
msgstr "This is the most core extension. Users do not need to manually write a set of `triton.Config`; instead, they can leave `configs` empty and let the Ascend backend automatically generate candidate configurations based on the kernel DSL semantics and runtime shapes."

msgid "2. 支持多个 config 的并行编译"
msgstr "2. Support parallel compilation of multiple configs"

msgid "当 autotune 需要评估多个候选配置时，Triton-Ascend 默认会并行编译这些候选配置，以缩短首次调优时延。"
msgstr "When autotune needs to evaluate multiple candidate configurations, Triton-Ascend compiles these candidate configurations in parallel by default to reduce the first-time tuning latency."

msgid "这一能力默认开启，可通过环境变量 `TRITON_AUTOTUNE_PARALLEL_COMPILE=0` 关闭。"
msgstr "This capability is enabled by default and can be disabled via the environment variable `TRITON_AUTOTUNE_PARALLEL_COMPILE=0`."

msgid "3. 支持使用 profiler 采集 kernel 性能"
msgstr "3. Supports using profiler to collect kernel performance."

msgid "Triton-Ascend 支持在 autotune 做 benchmark 时切换性能采集方式：除了默认 benchmark 模式外，还可以使用 profiler 来采集每个候选 config 的 kernel 性能数据，它只关注 kernel 的片上计算时间，对于执行时间较短的 kernel 比默认性能采集方式更加精确，但会增加一些耗时。这项能力可通过环境变量 `TRITON_BENCH_METHOD='npu'` 开启。"
msgstr "Triton-Ascend supports switching performance collection methods during autotune benchmarking: in addition to the default benchmark mode, a profiler can be used to collect kernel performance data for each candidate config. It focuses only on the on-chip computation time of the kernel, providing higher accuracy than the default performance collection method for kernels with short execution times, though it adds some overhead. This capability can be enabled via the environment variable `TRITON_BENCH_METHOD='npu'`."

msgid "自动 Tiling 生成能力的范围与行为"
msgstr "Scope and Behavior of Automatic Tiling Generation Capability"

msgid "前面的第 1 点说明了 Triton-Ascend 支持 `configs=[]` 自动生成候选配置。对这项能力，进行以下几点说明。"
msgstr "The first point above explains that Triton-Ascend supports `configs=[]` for automatically generating candidate configurations. The following points elaborate on this capability."

msgid "1. 自动生成范围聚焦在 Tiling 参数"
msgstr "The auto-generation scope focuses on Tiling parameters."

msgid "Ascend 自动生成的重点是 kernel 中与 Tiling 相关的 `tl.constexpr` 参数，也就是影响每个 block（逻辑核）处理的数据规模或 tile 大小的参数。"
msgstr "The focus of Ascend's automatic generation is the `tl.constexpr` parameters related to Tiling in the kernel, that is, the parameters that affect the data size or tile size processed by each block (logical core)."

msgid "这套能力不等价于“自动帮你调所有参数”。像 `num_warps`、`num_stages` 这类编译参数，以及 kernel 的非 Tiling 参数，不属于当前自动生成范围。"
msgstr "This capability is not equivalent to \"automatically tuning all parameters for you.\" Compilation parameters such as `num_warps` and `num_stages`, as well as non-tiling parameters of the kernel, are not within the current scope of automatic generation."

msgid "2. 候选配置会带上 Ascend 硬件约束"
msgstr "2. Candidate configurations will carry Ascend hardware constraints."

msgid "Ascend backend 在生成候选时，会结合 NPU 的片上存储容量、对齐约束、核数利用等边界做筛选，而不是单纯枚举一批配置再盲目 benchmark。"
msgstr "When generating candidates, the Ascend backend filters based on constraints such as NPU on-chip memory capacity, alignment constraints, and core utilization, rather than simply enumerating a set of configurations and blindly benchmarking."

msgid "3. 自动 Tiling 模式的目标是方便给出“性能不错”的配置"
msgstr "3. The goal of the automatic tiling mode is to conveniently provide a configuration with \"good performance.\""

msgid "为了权衡寻优时间和寻优效果，当前自动 Tiling 会对生成配置数量做大量剪枝，因此并不保证自动生成结果一定能达到手工极致调优的性能上限。"
msgstr "To balance optimization time and optimization effectiveness, current automatic Tiling performs extensive pruning on the number of generated configurations, so it does not guarantee that the automatically generated results will necessarily achieve the performance upper bound of manual extreme tuning."

msgid "这项能力的目标，是在尽量降低用户使用门槛和寻优成本的前提下，方便地给用户提供一个性能还不错的 Tiling 配置。"
msgstr "The goal of this capability is to conveniently provide users with a Tiling configuration that offers decent performance, while minimizing the user's usage threshold and optimization cost."

msgid "4. 自动 Tiling 生成失败时需要用户手写 `triton.Config`"
msgstr "4. When automatic tiling generation fails, the user needs to manually write `triton.Config`."

msgid "如果自动 Tiling 模式无法生成任何可用候选配置，这时需要用户改为手写 `triton.Config`。同时也建议对这类场景提 issue，帮助 Triton-Ascend 后续补齐解析和自动生成能力。"
msgstr "If the automatic Tiling mode fails to generate any usable candidate configurations, users need to manually write `triton.Config` instead. It is also recommended to submit an issue for such scenarios to help Triton-Ascend improve parsing and automatic generation capabilities in the future."

msgid "手写 `triton.Config` 模式"
msgstr "Handwritten `triton.Config` mode"

msgid "如果自动 Tiling 模式生成失败，或生成的 Tiling 性能未达到预期，直接回到社区标准写法即可。Triton-Ascend 对这部分语义保持兼容："
msgstr "If the automatic Tiling mode generation fails, or the generated Tiling performance does not meet expectations, simply revert to the community standard implementation. Triton-Ascend maintains compatibility with this part of the semantics."

msgid "这一模式下："
msgstr "In this mode:"

msgid "配置由用户手工提供；"
msgstr "The configuration is manually provided by the user."

msgid "框架负责 benchmark、选择最优配置和缓存复用；"
msgstr "The framework is responsible for benchmarking, selecting the optimal configuration, and cache reuse."

msgid "使用习惯与社区 autotune 保持一致。"
msgstr "Usage habits are consistent with the community autotune."

msgid "进阶用法：自动 Tiling 与其他参数联合调优"
msgstr "Advanced Usage: Automatic Tiling Combined with Other Parameter Tuning"

msgid "以下内容属于进阶用法，只有当用户希望在自动 Tiling 模式下，继续联合调优 kernel 的非 Tiling 参数或编译参数时，再考虑使用。"
msgstr "The following content pertains to advanced usage, which should only be considered when the user wishes to continue jointly tuning non-Tiling parameters or compilation parameters of the kernel under automatic Tiling mode."

msgid "1. 社区 autotune：手工枚举全部调优参数"
msgstr "Community autotune: manually enumerating all tuning parameters"

msgid "社区标准写法是由用户手工枚举所有候选配置："
msgstr "The standard community practice is for users to manually enumerate all candidate configurations."

msgid "2. Triton-Ascend：手工枚举 Tiling 参数和 Ascend 编译参数"
msgstr "2. Triton-Ascend: Manual Enumeration of Tiling Parameters and Ascend Compilation Parameters"

msgid "在 Triton-Ascend 中，如果希望继续走手工枚举模式，也可以把 Ascend 侧参数一起放进手工配置空间："
msgstr "In Triton-Ascend, if you wish to continue using the manual enumeration mode, you can also include the Ascend-side parameters together in the manual configuration space."

msgid "3. Triton-Ascend：自动生成 Tiling，同时联合调优其他参数"
msgstr "3. Triton-Ascend: Automatically generates Tiling while jointly optimizing other parameters."

msgid "如果希望 Tiling 参数继续由 `configs=[]` 自动生成，但又希望同时调优其他非 Tiling 参数或编译参数，可以把这些额外搜索维度通过 `hints` 传入："
msgstr "If you want the Tiling parameters to continue being automatically generated by `configs=[]`, but also wish to tune other non-Tiling parameters or compilation parameters simultaneously, you can pass these additional search dimensions via `hints`:"

msgid "这种方式的含义是："
msgstr "The meaning of this approach is:"

msgid "Tiling 相关参数仍然由 Triton-Ascend 自动生成；"
msgstr "Tiling-related parameters are still automatically generated by Triton-Ascend."

msgid "非 Tiling 参数或编译参数由用户通过 `hints` 显式给出候选集合；"
msgstr "Non-tiling parameters or compilation parameters are explicitly provided by the user as candidate sets through `hints`."

msgid "autotune 会对两部分组合后的配置空间做评估。"
msgstr "autotune evaluates the configuration space after combining the two parts."

msgid "小结"
msgstr "Summary"

msgid "Triton-Ascend 相比社区 autotune 的关键扩展，不是改变用户接口，而是在社区接口之上增加了“自动生成 Tiling 候选并完成寻优”的能力。对大多数用户来说，最推荐的使用方式就是："
msgstr "The key extension of Triton-Ascend compared to the community autotune is not changing the user interface, but adding the capability to \"automatically generate Tiling candidates and complete optimization\" on top of the community interface. For most users, the most recommended usage is:"

msgid "保持社区版 `@triton.autotune` 的写法；"
msgstr "Keep the writing style of the community edition `@triton.autotune`."

msgid "将 `configs` 设为 `[]`；"
msgstr "Set `configs` to `[]`."

msgid "让 Ascend backend 基于 kernel DSL 和运行时 shape 自动完成候选生成、筛选、benchmark 与缓存复用。"
msgstr "Enable the Ascend backend to automatically perform candidate generation, filtering, benchmarking, and cache reuse based on the kernel DSL and runtime shape."

msgid "如果场景不适合自动 Tiling 模式，再回到手写 `triton.Config` 即可。"
msgstr "If the scenario is not suitable for the automatic Tiling mode, simply return to manually writing `triton.Config`."

msgid "贡献者公约"
msgstr "Contributor Covenant"

msgid "我们的承诺"
msgstr "Our Commitment"

msgid "我们承诺使我们的社区对所有人保持友好、安全且公平。"
msgstr "We are committed to keeping our community friendly, safe, and fair for everyone."

msgid "我们承诺营造一个尊重并促进每位个体尊严、权利与贡献的环境，无论其种族、民族、种姓、肤色、年龄、体貌特征、神经多样性、残疾状况、生理性别或社会性别、性别认同或表达、性取向、语言、哲学或宗教信仰、国籍或社会出身、社会经济地位、教育程度或其他身份属性。所有真诚参与并遵守本公约者，均享有同等的参与权利。"
msgstr "We are committed to fostering an environment that respects and promotes the dignity, rights, and contributions of every individual, regardless of race, ethnicity, caste, skin color, age, physical appearance, neurodiversity, disability status, sex or gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, language, philosophical or religious beliefs, nationality or social origin, socioeconomic status, educational background, or other identity attributes. All individuals who sincerely participate and adhere to this covenant are entitled to equal participation rights."

msgid "受鼓励的行为"
msgstr "Encouraged behaviors"

msgid "虽然各自的社会规范可能有差异，但我们都努力达到这个社区对积极行为的期待。我们也了解，因为文化、背景或母语的不同，别人对我们的言行的解读可能不同于我们的初衷。"
msgstr "Although our social norms may differ, we all strive to meet this community's expectations for positive behavior. We also understand that due to differences in culture, background, or native language, others may interpret our words and actions differently from our original intentions."

msgid "考虑到以上这些，我们承诺以审慎的态度彼此相待，并以践行以下共同价值为行为准则："
msgstr "Considering the above, we commit to treating each other with prudence and adhering to the following shared values as our code of conduct:"

msgid "尊重我们**社区的宗旨**、各项活动及集会方式"
msgstr "Respect the **purpose** of our community, its activities, and its ways of gathering."

msgid "以**善意与诚实**的态度与他人互动"
msgstr "Interact with others with **goodwill and honesty**."

msgid "尊重**不同的观点与经历**"
msgstr "Respect **different perspectives and experiences**"

msgid "对自己的言行及贡献**负责**"
msgstr "Take **responsibility** for your own words, actions, and contributions."

msgid "以得体的方式给予并接受**建设性意见**"
msgstr "Give and receive **constructive feedback** in a professional manner."

msgid "承诺在造成伤害时进行**弥补**"
msgstr "Promise to **make amends** when harm is caused"

msgid "采取其他有益于**社区福祉**的行为"
msgstr "Take other actions that benefit **community well-being**."

msgid "受限制的行为"
msgstr "Restricted Behaviors"

msgid "我们同意在社区内限制以下行为。出现这些行为、威胁实施这些行为、或宣传这些行为，均视为违反本行为准则。"
msgstr "We agree to restrict the following behaviors within the community. Engaging in these behaviors, threatening to engage in them, or promoting them is considered a violation of this Code of Conduct."

msgid "**骚扰**：在明确表达界限后仍侵犯这些界限，或在被清楚要求停止后，仍进行不必要的个人关注。"
msgstr "**Harassment**: Continuing to violate boundaries after they have been clearly expressed, or giving unwanted personal attention after being explicitly asked to stop."

msgid "**人身攻击**：针对社区成员或群体发表侮辱、贬低或带有蔑视性的言论。"
msgstr "**Personal Attacks**: Making insulting, demeaning, or contemptuous remarks toward community members or groups."

msgid "**刻板印象或歧视**：基于无法改变的身份或特征，来评判他人的性格或行为。"
msgstr "**Stereotypes or Discrimination**: Judging others' character or behavior based on unchangeable identities or traits."

msgid "**性化**：做出在社区场景或宗旨下普遍认为不恰当的亲密举动。"
msgstr "**Sexualization**: Engaging in intimate actions that are generally considered inappropriate within the community context or under its guiding principles."

msgid "**侵犯保密性**：未经允许分享或利用他人的个人或隐私信息。"
msgstr "**Breach of Confidentiality**: Sharing or exploiting others' personal or private information without authorization."

msgid "**危害行为**：对任何人或群体实施、煽动或威胁施加暴力及其他伤害。"
msgstr "**Harmful Behavior**: Committing, inciting, or threatening violence and other harm against any person or group."

msgid "其他威胁**社区福祉**的行为。"
msgstr "Other behaviors that threaten **community well-being**."

msgid "其他限制行为"
msgstr "Other restrictions on conduct"

msgid "**虚假身份**：出于任何原因冒充他人，或假扮他人以规避监管措施。"
msgstr "**False Identity**: Impersonating others for any reason, or pretending to be someone else to circumvent regulatory measures."

msgid "**未正确标明来源**：未正确标明所贡献内容的来源。"
msgstr "**Incorrectly attributed source**: The source of the contributed content is not properly cited."

msgid "**宣传材料**：以不符合社区规范的方式分享营销或其他商业内容。"
msgstr "**Promotional Materials**: Sharing marketing or other commercial content in a manner that does not comply with community guidelines."

msgid "**不当传播**：未能以负责任的方式呈现包含、链接或描述任何其他受限制行为的内容。"
msgstr "**Improper Dissemination**: Failure to present content that includes, links to, or describes any other restricted behavior in a responsible manner."

msgid "通报问题"
msgstr "Report the issue"

msgid "即使社区成员之间尽其所能地合作，也仍然可能发生矛盾。并不是所有冲突都涉及违反行为准则，本准则旨在强化受鼓励的行为与规范，它们有助于预防冲突并将伤害降到最低。"
msgstr "Even when community members collaborate to the best of their abilities, conflicts may still arise. Not all conflicts involve violations of the code of conduct; this code aims to reinforce encouraged behaviors and norms, which help prevent conflicts and minimize harm."

msgid "当事件发生时，及时报告非常重要。要报告可能的违规行为，**[注意：请在此填入举报方式]**。"
msgstr "When an incident occurs, timely reporting is very important. To report potential violations, **[Note: Please fill in the reporting method here]**."

msgid "社区管理员会严肃对待违规报告，并尽力及时回应。将对所有违反行为准则的报告展开调查，方式包括查阅消息、日志及录音，或访谈证人及其他相关参与人。社区管理员在优先保障安全与保密性的前提下，会尽可能保持调查与执行过程的透明度。为践行这些价值观，执行措施会在涉事各方的私下环境中进行，但如经各方同意，将事件通报全体社区也可以作为解决方案的一部分。"
msgstr "Community administrators take violation reports seriously and strive to respond in a timely manner. All reports of violations of the code of conduct will be investigated, which may involve reviewing messages, logs, and recordings, or interviewing witnesses and other relevant participants. While prioritizing safety and confidentiality, community administrators will maintain transparency in the investigation and enforcement process to the greatest extent possible. To uphold these values, enforcement measures will be carried out in a private setting involving the relevant parties; however, with the consent of all parties, notifying the entire community about the incident may also be part of the resolution."

msgid "处理与弥补伤害"
msgstr "Handle and remedy harm"

msgid "**[注意：下文所列的处理办法与补救措施，是基于行为准则执行过程中的最佳做法而提出的建议。如果你们的社区已经有既定的执行流程，请确保修改本段内容，以描述你们自己的政策。]**"
msgstr "**[Note: The handling methods and remedial measures listed below are recommendations based on best practices in the enforcement of the Code of Conduct. If your community already has an established enforcement process, please ensure that this section is modified to describe your own policies.]**"

msgid "若社区管理员经调查确认存在违反此行为准则的行为，将参照以下\"分级处理\"机制，根据事件对相关人员及社区整体造成的影响程度，确定最适宜的伤害弥补方案。根据违规严重程度，可跳过较低级别的处理措施。"
msgstr "If the community administrator confirms through investigation that there has been a violation of this Code of Conduct, the most appropriate remedy for the harm caused will be determined based on the \"Progressive Action\" mechanism outlined below, taking into account the impact of the incident on the individuals involved and the community as a whole. Depending on the severity of the violation, lower-level corrective measures may be bypassed."

msgid "警告"
msgstr "Warning"

msgid "**事件**：单次或连续违规行为"
msgstr "**Event**: A single or continuous violation"

msgid "**后果**：社区管理员将发出书面私信警告"
msgstr "**Consequence**: The community administrator will issue a written private message warning."

msgid "**弥补**：弥补的方式如书面私下致歉、坦承自己的责任，或主动确认清楚今后该如何做才符合期待。"
msgstr "**Remedy**: Ways to remedy include offering a written private apology, acknowledging one's responsibility, or proactively clarifying how to meet expectations in the future."

msgid "暂时限制活动"
msgstr "Temporarily restrict activity"

msgid "**事件**：重复造成先前已被警告的违规，或首次发生略为严重的违规行为。"
msgstr "**Event**: Repeated violations that have been previously warned, or a first occurrence of a slightly serious violation."

msgid "**后果**：发出私下的书面警告，并设定一个有时间限制的冷静期，旨在强调事态的严重性，并让相关社区成员有时间消化与处理该事件。冷静期可能是限制在特定的交流渠道，或限制与特定社区成员的互动。"
msgstr "**Consequence**: Issue a private written warning and set a time-limited cooling-off period, aimed at emphasizing the severity of the situation and allowing the relevant community member time to process and reflect on the incident. The cooling-off period may be restricted to specific communication channels or limited to interactions with particular community members."

msgid "**弥补**：修复的方式可能包括道歉、利用冷静期反思自身行为及其影响，以及充分意识到在冷静期结束后如何重新进入社区空间。"
msgstr "**Remediation**: Methods of repair may include apologizing, using a cooling-off period to reflect on one’s own behavior and its impact, and fully understanding how to re-enter the community space after the cooling-off period ends."

msgid "暂时停权"
msgstr "Temporary suspension"

msgid "**事件**：出现社区管理员已多次警告后仍然重复违规的模式，或一次严重违规行为。"
msgstr "**Event**: A pattern of repeated violations after multiple warnings from community administrators, or a single severe violation."

msgid "**后果**：发出私下的书面警告，并附上恢复权限所需满足的条件。通常，临时停权旨在给予被停权者时间，反思其行为以及考虑可能的改正措施。"
msgstr "**Consequences**: Issue a private written warning, along with the conditions required to restore permissions. Typically, a temporary suspension is intended to give the suspended party time to reflect on their behavior and consider possible corrective measures."

msgid "**弥补**：弥补的条件包括尊重停权的意旨、达成恢复权限的指定条件，以及充分认识到在停权解除后如何重新融入社区。"
msgstr "**Remedy**: Conditions for remedy include respecting the intent of the suspension, meeting the specified conditions for reinstatement of privileges, and fully understanding how to reintegrate into the community after the suspension is lifted."

msgid "永久封禁"
msgstr "Permanent ban"

msgid "**事件**：多次违反行为准则，且其他分级处理措施均未能解决问题，或发生严重到社区管理员认定无法在该成员继续存在的情况下保障社区安全的违规行为。"
msgstr "**Event**: Repeated violations of the code of conduct where other tiered measures have failed to resolve the issue, or a violation so severe that the community administrator determines that the safety of the community cannot be ensured with the member's continued presence."

msgid "**后果**：撤销其对所有社区空间、工具及交流渠道的访问权限。一般而言，永久封禁应极少使用，必须有充分且有力的理由，且仅在其他弥补手段未能改变其行为时才作为最后手段实施。"
msgstr "**Consequence**: Revoke their access to all community spaces, tools, and communication channels. Generally, permanent bans should be used sparingly, must have sufficient and compelling reasons, and should only be implemented as a last resort when other remedial measures have failed to change their behavior."

msgid "**弥补**：此类严重情形下，不存在可行的弥补途径。"
msgstr "**Mitigation**: In such severe cases, there are no feasible mitigation approaches."

msgid "本分级处理措施旨在作为指导方针，并不限制社区管理者在符合社区最大利益的前提下，运用其自主裁量权与判断力。"
msgstr "These tiered moderation measures are intended as guidelines and do not restrict community managers from exercising their discretion and judgment in the best interests of the community."

msgid "施行范围"
msgstr "Scope of Implementation"

msgid "本行为准则适用于社区所有空间，同时也适用于个人在公共场合或其他场合正式代表社区的情况。代表社区的行为包括但不限于：使用官方电子邮件地址；通过官方社交媒体账号发布内容；作为指定代表出席线上或线下活动。"
msgstr "This Code of Conduct applies to all community spaces and also applies when an individual is officially representing the community in public or other settings. Examples of representing the community include, but are not limited to: using an official email address; posting via official social media accounts; acting as a designated representative at online or offline events."

msgid "贡献归属"
msgstr "Attribution of Contributions"

msgid "本行为准则改编自 贡献者公约 3.0 版，该公约永久可在此查阅：[https://www.contributor-covenant.org/version/3/0/](https://www.contributor-covenant.org/version/3/0/)。"
msgstr "This Code of Conduct is adapted from the Contributor Covenant version 3.0, which is permanently available at: [https://www.contributor-covenant.org/version/3/0/](https://www.contributor-covenant.org/version/3/0/)."

msgid "贡献者公约 由 Organization for Ethical Source 负责维护，并以 CC BY-SA 4.0 许可协议发布。查看该许可协议请访问：[https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)。"
msgstr "Contributor Covenant is maintained by the Organization for Ethical Source and is published under the CC BY-SA 4.0 license. To view this license, please visit: [https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)."

msgid "关于 贡献者公约 的常见问题解答，请参阅：[https://www.contributor-covenant.org/faq](https://www.contributor-covenant.org/faq)。各语言版本译文请见：[https://www.contributor-covenant.org/translations](https://www.contributor-covenant.org/translations)。更多执行与社区指南资源请见：[https://www.contributor-covenant.org/resources](https://www.contributor-covenant.org/resources)。本分级措施的灵感来源于 [Mozilla 行为准则团队](https://github.com/mozilla/inclusion) 的工作。"
msgstr "For frequently asked questions about the Contributor Covenant, please see: [https://www.contributor-covenant.org/faq](https://www.contributor-covenant.org/faq). Translations in various languages are available at: [https://www.contributor-covenant.org/translations](https://www.contributor-covenant.org/translations). For additional resources on enforcement and community guidelines, please visit: [https://www.contributor-covenant.org/resources](https://www.contributor-covenant.org/resources). This graduated enforcement approach is inspired by the work of the [Mozilla Code of Conduct Team](https://github.com/mozilla/inclusion)."

