msgid "投票规则"
msgstr "Voting Rules"

msgid "未出席会议的 `Maintainer` 须在会议后 3 个工作日内提交投票；逾期未投票视为弃权"
msgstr "`Maintainers` who are absent from the meeting must submit their votes within 3 working days after the meeting; failure to vote within this period will be considered abstention."

msgid "投票通过条件为参与投票的 `Maintainer` 超过半数同意（弃权不计入投票总数）"
msgstr "The condition for passing a vote is that more than half of the participating `Maintainer` agree (abstentions are not counted in the total votes)."

msgid "投票结果记录于会议纪要中"
msgstr "The voting results are recorded in the meeting minutes."

msgid "决策流程"
msgstr "Decision-making process"

msgid "常规决策"
msgstr "Routine decision-making"

msgid "日常开发中的常规决策（如 `Bug` 修复、小功能改进）由相关模块的 `Maintainer` 在 `Issue` 或 `PR` 中审阅决定，无需召开会议。"
msgstr "Routine decisions in daily development (such as `Bug` fixes and minor feature improvements) are reviewed and decided by the `Maintainer` of the relevant module in the `Issue` or `PR`, without the need for a meeting."

msgid "重大决策"
msgstr "Major decision"

msgid "以下事项视为重大决策，需由 `Maintainer` 在社区技术会议中集体讨论："
msgstr "The following matters are considered major decisions and require collective discussion by the `Maintainer` in the community technical meeting."

msgid "重大架构变更"
msgstr "Major architectural changes"

msgid "破坏性 `API` 变更"
msgstr "Breaking `API` Changes"

msgid "新增核心功能或移除现有功能"
msgstr "Added core features or removed existing features"

msgid "第三方依赖的重大升级"
msgstr "Major upgrade of third-party dependencies"

msgid "版本发布规划"
msgstr "Version Release Planning"

msgid "重大决策流程："
msgstr "Major Decision-Making Process:"

msgid "提交 `RFC`（征求意见稿），描述变更内容、影响范围和实施方案"
msgstr "Submit the `RFC` (Request for Comments) describing the changes, scope of impact, and implementation plan."

msgid "在技术会议中讨论"
msgstr "Discussing in a technical meeting"

msgid "`Maintainer` 共同决策"
msgstr "`Maintainer` co-decision"

msgid "Roadmap指导"
msgstr "Roadmap guidance"

msgid "使用 GitHub Issue 来跟踪和管理各组织的计划及中长期目标。本文档为社区项目编写路线图类 Issue 提供参考和规范，以帮助创建和维护高质量的路线图。"
msgstr "Use GitHub Issues to track and manage the plans and medium-to-long-term goals of each organization. This document provides references and guidelines for writing roadmap-type Issues in community projects, helping to create and maintain high-quality roadmaps."

