msgstr "Optimized code:"

msgid "动态计算适合的 BLOCK_SIZE 以避免 coreDim 超限"
msgstr "Dynamically calculate the appropriate BLOCK_SIZE to avoid exceeding the coreDim limit."

msgid "处理复合问题：coreDim + UB 溢出"
msgstr "Handling composite issues: coreDim + UB overflow"

msgid "问题分析: 在某些情况下，解决了 coreDim 问题后可能引发新的UB溢出问题。这通常发生在增大 BLOCK_SIZE 后，单个线程块需要处理的数据量超出了NPU的UB缓存容量。"
msgstr "Problem Analysis: In some cases, resolving the coreDim issue may introduce new UB overflow problems. This typically occurs when increasing BLOCK_SIZE causes the amount of data processed by a single thread block to exceed the NPU's UB cache capacity."

msgid "案例： 数据规模：N = 1073741824，原始 BLOCK_SIZE = 4096，计算得到的 coreDim = 262144 > 65535（超限），调整为 BLOCK_SIZE = 32768 后，coreDim = 32768（合规），但出现 UB 溢出"
msgstr "Case: Data size: N = 1073741824, original BLOCK_SIZE = 4096, calculated coreDim = 262144 > 65535 (out of range). After adjusting BLOCK_SIZE = 32768, coreDim = 32768 (compliant), but UB overflow occurs."

msgid "解决思路： 引入 BLOCK_SIZE_SUB 参数，将大块进一步细分，在保持合理 coreDim 的同时控制内存使用。 优化前代码："
msgstr "Solution: Introduce the BLOCK_SIZE_SUB parameter to further subdivide large blocks, controlling memory usage while maintaining a reasonable coreDim. Code before optimization:"

msgid "优化后代码："
msgstr "Optimized code:"

msgid "为什么会出现UBSIZE超出内存的错误"
msgstr "Why does the UBSIZE exceed memory error occur?"

msgid "切分不合理,存在过多的非对齐访存或者运算，例如对（64，32）二维数据搬运，对应stride(12832，128),如果是对齐数据的访存，对应的stride(32,1)。 对于非对齐访问内容，在最内轴新增一个大小为1的轴，变为（64，32，4） 由于硬件要求vector算子场景ub内存32bytes对齐 ，假设type=float16，对应stride应该为(12832, 128,1)"
msgstr "The segmentation is unreasonable, with excessive non-aligned memory accesses or operations. For example, when moving 2D data of (64, 32), the corresponding stride is (12832, 128). If it is aligned memory access, the corresponding stride should be (32, 1). For non-aligned access content, add a new axis of size 1 to the innermost axis, changing it to (64, 32, 4). Due to the hardware requirement that UB memory must be 32-byte aligned in vector operator scenarios, assuming type=float16, the corresponding stride should be (12832, 128, 1)."

msgid "离散访存代码逐行对比观察scalar低效映射"
msgstr "Discrete memory access code line-by-line comparison observes scalar inefficient mapping"

msgid "设置环境变量TRITON_DEBUG=1, 保存~/.triton/cache/xxx.ttadapter，然后执行"
msgstr "Set the environment variable `TRITON_DEBUG=1`, save `~/.triton/cache/xxx.ttadapter`, and then execute."

msgid "会有输出IR ， 对比Triton 算子逻辑与IR内部的操作，观察是否有未映射成指令的操作。 观察HIVM IR阶段是否存在纯scalar搬运或者计算， 没有映射为simd指令，这会成为性能瓶颈。"
msgstr "There will be an output IR. Compare the Triton operator logic with the operations inside the IR to observe if there are any operations not mapped to instructions. Observe whether there are pure scalar transfers or computations in the HIVM IR stage that are not mapped to SIMD instructions, as this could become a performance bottleneck."

msgid "问题：离散访存 && scalar低效映射 b[1024, 32] = a[1024, 32]  Triton原先写法利用thread的方式 对[1024,32] 中的最低维度32绑定线程块, 再对1024切16，分为[64， 16， 32]，再对64绑定线程块"
msgstr "Problem: Disjoint memory access && scalar inefficient mapping b[1024, 32] = a[1024, 32]. The original Triton implementation uses a thread-based approach, binding the lowest dimension 32 in [1024, 32] to thread blocks, then splitting 1024 into 16, resulting in [64, 16, 32], and finally binding 64 to thread blocks."

msgid "优化思路"
msgstr "Optimization Approach"

msgid "调整 block_ptr 的 shape/stride: 把 (1024, 32) 看成二维矩阵，最低维度 32 是连续的，所以 stride 应该是 (32, 1)，而不是 (32,)，这样每个线程块能访问连续的 32 元素。让线程块绑定到行维度（1024），每个线程处理一整行的 32 元素。这样访存就是连续的，亲和性好。"
msgstr "Adjust the shape/stride of block_ptr: treat (1024, 32) as a 2D matrix, where the lowest dimension 32 is contiguous, so the stride should be (32, 1) instead of (32,), allowing each thread block to access contiguous 32 elements. Bind the thread block to the row dimension (1024), with each thread processing an entire row of 32 elements. This makes memory access contiguous and improves affinity."

msgid "比如："
msgstr "For example:"

msgid "NPU高性能编程指南"
msgstr "NPU High-Performance Programming Guide"

msgid "合并Grid分核"
msgstr "Merge Grid Subdivision"

msgid "一、自动合并Grid分核优化原则"
msgstr "I. Principles of Automatic Merging Grid Core Optimization"

msgid "部分场景下，Triton算子从GPU迁移到NPU。由于体系结构的差异，基于GPU开发的Triton算子Grid分核数较多。在NPU上执行时，无法一次全部调度，多轮下发导致下发时延过大，影响算子性能。基于NPU优Triton算子过程中，需要首先检查Grid分核数。当分核数较大时，使用TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL环境变量提升算子执行性能。"
msgstr "In some scenarios, Triton operators are migrated from GPU to NPU. Due to architectural differences, Triton operators developed on GPU have a large number of grid blocks. When executed on NPU, they cannot be fully scheduled in one go, and multiple rounds of dispatch lead to excessive dispatch latency, affecting operator performance. During the optimization of Triton operators on NPU, it is necessary to first check the number of grid blocks. When the number of blocks is large, use the `TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL` environment variable to improve operator execution performance."

msgid "指令并行优化"
msgstr "Instruction-Level Parallelism Optimization"

msgid "一、指令并行优化核心原则"
msgstr "I. Core Principles of Instruction Parallelism Optimization"

msgid "Triton算子在NPU上执行时，为了提升性能，NPU底层提供multi buffer、指令并行等并行机制，将“数据搬入/数据计算/数据搬出”并行起来，以此来提升性能；但是某些场景下存在multi buffer无法使能问题，影响并行度，导致算子执行性能降低；在性能优化过程中，存在此类问题时，可以参考以下几点做排查，并按照代码示例优化： 1、数据搬运和计算存在数据依赖，产生同步，必须依赖Vector运算后，才能触发MTE搬运，导致并行度低； 2、算子内，无多个数据加载或者单次执行完成无Tiling切分，该场景下无法使能multi buffer； 3、multi buffer需要额外增加UB空间的使用，计算过程中UB空间不足，无法使能multi buffer；"
msgstr "When Triton operators execute on the NPU, to improve performance, the NPU underlying layer provides parallel mechanisms such as multi-buffer and instruction parallelism, which parallelize \"data loading / data computation / data unloading\" to enhance performance. However, in some scenarios, multi-buffer cannot be enabled, affecting parallelism and leading to reduced operator execution performance. During performance optimization, when such issues arise, you can refer to the following points for troubleshooting and optimize according to the code examples: 1. Data loading and computation have data dependencies, causing synchronization. MTE loading can only be triggered after Vector computation is completed, resulting in low parallelism; 2. Within the operator, there is no multiple data loading or no Tiling division after a single execution, making multi-buffer unable to be enabled in this scenario; 3. Multi-buffer requires additional UB space usage. If UB space is insufficient during computation, multi-buffer cannot be enabled."

msgid "二、代码示例"
msgstr "2. Code Example"

msgid "示例1：减少同步，提升并行度"
msgstr "Example 1: Reduce synchronization and increase parallelism"

msgid "在算子调优过程中，增加指令并行度是算子调优的重要手段。在如下的tl.load语句中，当N > M时, load加载的数据只能填充部分data指向的tensor内存空间中，剩下未填充的部分，如果用户未指定other值，则GPU默认填充为0，为了减少用户迁移的适配工作，NPU保持行为和GPU一致。NPU会先用Vector核对data指向的全部内存空间设置为指定值(如果用户未指定other值，同样设置为0)，然后在使用MTE2指令搬运数据到data指向的部分内存空间，这样就会导致MTE2和Vector产生依赖，无法高效并行，影响性能："
msgstr "During operator tuning, increasing instruction-level parallelism is an important approach. In the following `tl.load` statement, when N > M, the loaded data can only fill part of the tensor memory space pointed to by `data`. For the remaining unfilled portion, if the user does not specify an `other` value, the GPU defaults to filling it with 0. To reduce the adaptation effort for user migration, the NPU maintains behavior consistent with the GPU. The NPU first uses Vector core to set the entire memory space pointed to by `data` to the specified value (if the user does not specify an `other` value, it is also set to 0), and then uses the MTE2 instruction to move data to the partially filled memory space pointed to by `data`. This creates a dependency between MTE2 and Vector, preventing efficient parallelism and impacting performance."

msgid "为了提升性能，在load加载数据只能部分填充到指向的内存空间时，如果未填充的部分不影响后续的计算结果，可以在load语句中，添加care_padding=False来去掉默认值的填充，增加并行度，提升性能，上面算子的优化写法如下："
msgstr "To improve performance, when the load operation only partially fills the pointed memory space, and the unfilled portion does not affect subsequent computation results, you can add `care_padding=False` to the load statement to remove default value padding, increase parallelism, and enhance performance. The optimized version of the above operator is as follows:"

msgid "示例2：在Triton算子内，使用for循环，增加Tiling，提升并行度"
msgstr "Example 2: Use a for loop within the Triton operator to add Tiling and improve parallelism."

msgid "在Triton算子编程中，mask运算经常运用在load/store/where等语法中，在性能优化过程中，需要特别注意这类运算导致的性能下降。当Triton算子内逻辑是单次顺序执行，开始->数据搬入->计算->数据搬出->结束，指令无法并行，执行效率低;可以通过在算子使用for循环增加tiling，将单次处理量减少，多次处理，能够让\"数据搬入/计算/数据搬出\"并行起来，减少串行的等待时间，提升整体性能；同时使用for循环增加Tiling，也能降低单次处理消耗的UB空间。   需要注意：增加数据Tiling也同时需要考虑改变数据切块后的数学是否等价。"
msgstr "In Triton operator programming, mask operations are frequently used in syntax such as load/store/where. During performance optimization, special attention must be paid to the performance degradation caused by such operations. When the logic within a Triton operator is a single sequential execution—start → data load → computation → data store → end—instructions cannot be parallelized, resulting in low execution efficiency. By using a for loop to add tiling in the operator, the single processing volume can be reduced, and multiple processing steps can parallelize \"data load/computation/data store,\" reducing serial waiting time and improving overall performance. Additionally, using a for loop to add tiling also reduces the UB space consumed by a single processing step. Note: When increasing data tiling, it is also necessary to consider whether the mathematics after changing the data partitioning remains equivalent."

msgid "数据类型优化"
msgstr "Data Type Optimization"

msgid "一、数据类型优化核心原则"
msgstr "1. Core Principles of Data Type Optimization"

msgid "A2/A3 向量运算单元的部分运算操作不支持某些数据类型，这种场景下，对应的向量运算会退化为标量运算，影响性能。在确定不影响整体算子精度的情况下，建议使用支持的数据类型，提升性能。 主要涉及以下操作"
msgstr "The A2/A3 vector arithmetic unit does not support certain data types for some operations. In such cases, the corresponding vector operations will degrade to scalar operations, impacting performance. If it is confirmed that the overall operator precision is not affected, it is recommended to use supported data types to improve performance. The main operations involved are as follows."

msgid "**OP名称**"
msgstr "**OP Name**"

msgid "**不支持的数据类型**"
msgstr "**Unsupported Data Types**"

msgid "Vector ADD"
msgstr "Vector ADD"

msgid "int64"
msgstr "int64"

msgid "Vector CMP"
msgstr "Vector CMP"

msgid "int64/int32"
msgstr "int64/int32"

msgid "Vector Add Triton算子示例代码"
msgstr "Vector Add Triton Operator Example Code"

msgid "如下Triton算子，当x, y input tensor使用的数据类型是int64时，会导致x1+y1运算展开为Scalar运算，降低性能，在不影响精度的情况下，建议使用int32数据类型。"
msgstr "For the following Triton operator, when the data type used by the x and y input tensors is int64, it will cause the x1 + y1 operation to be expanded into scalar operations, reducing performance. Without affecting precision, it is recommended to use the int32 data type."

msgid "Vector Cmp Triton算子示例代码"
msgstr "Vector Cmp Triton Operator Example Code"

msgid "如下Triton算子，做mask运算时，使用到了Cmp操作，Cmp不支持int64/int32数据类型，会导致cols < N运算展开为Scalar运算，降低性能，在不影响精度的情况下，建议使用fp32数据类型。   在Triton算子编程中，mask运算经常运用在load/store/where等语法中，在性能优化过程中，需要特别注意这类运算导致的性能下降。"
msgstr "For the following Triton operator, the Cmp operation is used during mask computation. Cmp does not support int64/int32 data types, which may cause the cols < N operation to be expanded into scalar operations, reducing performance. Without affecting precision, it is recommended to use the fp32 data type. In Triton operator programming, mask operations are often used in syntax such as load/store/where. During performance optimization, special attention should be paid to the performance degradation caused by such operations."

msgid "Cube 算子开发"
msgstr "Cube operator development"

msgid "Cube 算子以矩阵乘或批量矩阵乘为主要计算负载，Triton 代码中通常以 `tl.dot` 为核心。Cube 算子的关键是围绕 M/N/K 三个维度设计 tile，使 A/B tile 能高效搬运到片上并在 Cube Core 上完成累加。"
msgstr "The Cube operator primarily uses matrix multiplication or batched matrix multiplication as its main computational workload, with `tl.dot` typically serving as the core in Triton code. The key to the Cube operator is designing tiles around the M/N/K dimensions, enabling efficient movement of A/B tiles onto the chip and completing accumulation on the Cube Core."

msgid "Cube 简单算子开发"
msgstr "Cube Simple Operator Development"

msgid "简单 Cube 算子可参考本仓 [矩阵乘法样例](../examples/05_matrix_multiplication_example.md)。一个最小开发路径包括："
msgstr "For a simple Cube operator, refer to the [matrix multiplication example](../examples/05_matrix_multiplication_example.md) in this repository. A minimal development path includes:"

msgid "明确输入输出 shape 和 stride，例如 `A[M, K]`、`B[K, N]`、`C[M, N]`。"
msgstr "Clearly define the input and output shapes and strides, such as `A[M, K]`, `B[K, N]`, `C[M, N]`."

msgid "用 `tl.program_id` 映射当前 program 到输出矩阵的 `(pid_m, pid_n)` tile。"
msgstr "Map the current program to the `(pid_m, pid_n)` tile of the output matrix using `tl.program_id`."

msgid "用 `BLOCK_SIZE_M/N/K` 构造 A/B 的二维偏移。"
msgstr "Construct the two-dimensional offsets of A/B using `BLOCK_SIZE_M/N/K`."

msgid "沿 K 维循环加载 A/B 子块，并用 `tl.dot` 累加到 fp32 accumulator。"
msgstr "Load A/B sub-blocks along the K dimension cyclically and accumulate them into the fp32 accumulator using `tl.dot`."

msgid "将 accumulator 转为输出 dtype，并用边界 mask 写回 C。"
msgstr "Convert the accumulator to the output dtype and write back to C using the boundary mask."

msgid "核心结构如下："
msgstr "The core structure is as follows:"

msgid "简单 Cube 算子调参时优先关注："
msgstr "When tuning parameters for a simple Cube operator, prioritize the following:"

msgid "`BLOCK_M/N/K` 是否满足硬件支持和 UB/L1 容量限制。"
msgstr "Whether `BLOCK_M/N/K` meets hardware support and UB/L1 capacity constraints."

msgid "K 维循环是否可以开启 `multibuffer` 以形成搬运和计算流水。"
msgstr "Whether the K-dimension loop can enable `multibuffer` to form a pipeline for data transfer and computation."

msgid "输出 tile 是否包含额外 bias、scale、activation。如果后处理很轻，可以仍归为 Cube 算子；如果后处理包含明显 Vector 归约或跨核同步，应按 CV 融合算子组织。"
msgstr "Whether the output tile includes additional bias, scale, or activation. If the post-processing is very lightweight, it can still be classified as a Cube operator; if the post-processing involves significant vector reduction or cross-core synchronization, it should be organized as a CV fusion operator."

msgid "Cube 复杂算子开发"
msgstr "Cube Complex Operator Development"

msgid "复杂 Cube 场景通常来自 attention、batched matmul、grouped matmul 或形状不规则的矩阵乘。当前 [Ascend/triton-ascend-ops](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops) 主分支的复杂案例集中在 `tutorial/best_practice/`，其中 [`002-decode_grouped_attention.py`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/002-decode_grouped_attention.py) 可以作为复杂 Cube 核心逻辑的参考：它包含 QK、PV 两段 `tl.dot`，并展示了 KV cache 离散索引下如何重组 K/V 访存。"
msgstr "Complex Cube scenarios typically arise from attention, batched matmul, grouped matmul, or irregularly shaped matrix multiplications. Currently, the complex cases on the main branch of [Ascend/triton-ascend-ops](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops) are concentrated in `tutorial/best_practice/`, where [`002-decode_grouped_attention.py`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/002-decode_grouped_attention.py) can serve as a reference for the core logic of complex Cube operations: it includes two `tl.dot` segments for QK and PV, and demonstrates how to reorganize K/V memory access under discrete KV cache indexing."

msgid "复杂 Cube 算子建议按以下顺序拆解："
msgstr "Complex Cube operators are recommended to be decomposed in the following order:"

msgid "**先抽出纯矩阵乘核心**：确认每次 `tl.dot` 的输入 tile shape、dtype、累加 dtype 和输出 tile shape。"
msgstr "**Extract the pure matrix multiplication core first**: Confirm the input tile shape, dtype, accumulation dtype, and output tile shape for each `tl.dot`."

msgid "**再处理不规则访存**：如果 K/V cache 低维离散、高维连续，直接二维 load 可能退化为标量访存。可先按连续维搬入 UB，再通过转置或 Ascend 扩展接口 `extension.insert_slice` 重组为 `tl.dot` 需要的布局。"
msgstr "**Reorganizing Irregular Memory Access**: If the K/V cache has low-dimensional discreteness and high-dimensional continuity, direct 2D load may degrade into scalar memory access. You can first load data into UB along the continuous dimension, then reorganize it into the layout required by `tl.dot` through transpose or the Ascend extension interface `extension.insert_slice`."

msgid "**把归约和归一化留到边界明确的位置**：例如 attention 中的 `max/sum/exp` 属于 Vector 逻辑，若和 `tl.dot` 放在同一 kernel，需要转到 [CV 融合算子开发](./cv_fusion_operator.md) 的思路。"
msgstr "**Leave reduction and normalization to boundary-clear positions**: For example, `max/sum/exp` in attention belongs to Vector logic. If placed in the same kernel as `tl.dot`, it needs to follow the approach of [CV fusion operator development](./cv_fusion_operator.md)."

msgid "**为长 K 或长序列设计内层循环**：K 维循环要控制单次 A/B tile 的片上占用；序列维循环要避免一次 load 过大的 K/V block。"
msgstr "**Designing Inner Loops for Long K or Long Sequences**: The K-dimension loop should control the on-chip occupancy of a single A/B tile; the sequence dimension loop should avoid loading an excessively large K/V block at once."

msgid "**用 Autotune 管理候选 tile**：为常见 shape 准备多组 `BLOCK_M/N/K` 和 `multibuffer` 配置，让运行时选择最优组合。"
msgstr "**Using Autotune to Manage Candidate Tiles**: Prepare multiple sets of `BLOCK_M/N/K` and `multibuffer` configurations for common shapes, allowing the runtime to select the optimal combination."

msgid "复杂 Cube 算子的常见风险是把 GPU 上的大量 program 直接迁移到 NPU。若输出 tile 数远大于物理 Cube Core 数，可考虑让每个 program 通过内层循环处理多个 tile，或者在确认逻辑核相互独立时设置 `TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL=1` 降低调度开销。"
msgstr "A common risk of complex Cube operators is directly migrating a large number of programs on GPU to NPU. If the number of output tiles is much larger than the number of physical Cube cores, consider having each program process multiple tiles through an inner loop, or set `TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL=1` to reduce scheduling overhead when logical cores are confirmed to be independent."

msgid "CV 融合算子开发"
msgstr "CV Fusion Operator Development"

msgid "CV 融合算子指同一个算子中同时使用 Cube Core 和 Vector Core：Cube Core 通常负责 `tl.dot`、矩阵乘或卷积式主计算，Vector Core 负责 bias、activation、softmax、归约、mask、layout 重排或跨块同步。CV 融合的目标是减少 kernel 边界和 GM 往返，但需要同时控制 Cube tile、Vector tile、UB/L1 占用和同步关系。"
msgstr "CV fusion operator refers to an operator that simultaneously uses Cube Core and Vector Core: Cube Core is typically responsible for `tl.dot`, matrix multiplication, or convolution-like main computations, while Vector Core handles bias, activation, softmax, reduction, mask, layout rearrangement, or cross-block synchronization. The goal of CV fusion is to reduce kernel boundaries and GM round trips, but it requires simultaneous control over Cube tile, Vector tile, UB/L1 occupancy, and synchronization relationships."

msgid "CV 融合简单算子开发"
msgstr "Development of Simple Operators for CV Fusion"

msgid "简单 CV 融合建议先从本仓 [矩阵乘法样例](../examples/05_matrix_multiplication_example.md) 抽出稳定的 `tl.dot` 主计算，再在写回前加入 Vector 后处理；更复杂的切片更新可参考 [融合注意力样例](../examples/04_fused_attention_example.md)。最小路径如下："
msgstr "For simple CV fusion, it is recommended to first extract the stable `tl.dot` main computation from the [matrix multiplication example](../examples/05_matrix_multiplication_example.md) in this repository, and then add Vector post-processing before writing back. For more complex slice updates, refer to the [fused attention example](../examples/04_fused_attention_example.md). The minimal path is as follows:"

msgid "先实现稳定的 Cube 主计算，例如 `acc = tl.dot(a, b, acc)`。"
msgstr "First implement the stable Cube main computation, such as `acc = tl.dot(a, b, acc)`."

msgid "在 accumulator 写回前融合轻量 Vector 后处理，例如 bias、scale、activation 或 dtype cast。"
msgstr "Fuse lightweight Vector post-processing before accumulator writeback, such as bias, scale, activation, or dtype cast."

msgid "对较大的 accumulator，可使用 `range` 配合 `extension.extract_slice`/`extension.insert_slice` 做普通子块切分，避免 Vector 后处理阶段 UB overflow。"
msgstr "For larger accumulators, `range` can be used with `extension.extract_slice`/`extension.insert_slice` for ordinary sub-block partitioning to avoid UB overflow during the Vector post-processing stage."

msgid "`extension.parallel(..., bind_sub_block=True)` 属于更强的显式多 Vector 子块绑定路径，目标硬件和编译配置存在差异时可能不可用，不建议作为简单示例的默认写法。"
msgstr "`extension.parallel(..., bind_sub_block=True)` is a stronger explicit multi-Vector sub-block binding path, which may not be available when the target hardware and compilation configuration differ. It is not recommended as the default writing style for simple examples."

msgid "示例结构："
msgstr "Example structure:"

msgid "简单 CV 融合开发时要保持边界清晰：Cube 负责产生较大的二维 accumulator，Vector 负责同一 tile 内的逐元素或小规模归约。若 Vector 部分需要跨多个 Cube tile 共享状态，就需要引入同步、workspace 或拆分 kernel。"
msgstr "When performing simple CV fusion development, keep boundaries clear: Cube is responsible for generating a larger two-dimensional accumulator, while Vector handles element-wise or small-scale reductions within the same tile. If the Vector part needs to share state across multiple Cube tiles, synchronization, workspace, or kernel splitting must be introduced."

msgid "CV 融合复杂算子开发"
msgstr "CV Fusion Complex Operator Development"

msgid "复杂 CV 融合可参考 [Ascend/triton-ascend-ops](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops) 中的 best practice："
msgstr "For complex CV fusion, refer to the best practice in [Ascend/triton-ascend-ops](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops)."

msgid "[`tutorial/best_practice/002-decode_grouped_attention.py`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/002-decode_grouped_attention.py)：Decode attention 中 QK/PV 使用 Cube，softmax、mask、指数、归一化和离散 KV 访存重排使用 Vector。"
msgstr "[`tutorial/best_practice/002-decode_grouped_attention.py`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/002-decode_grouped_attention.py): In Decode attention, QK/PV uses Cube, while softmax, mask, exponentiation, normalization, and discrete KV memory access reordering use Vector."

msgid "[`tutorial/best_practice/003-fused-cat-slice-conv1d.zh.md`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/003-fused-cat-slice-conv1d.zh.md)：展示融合 cat、slice、conv1d update 时如何用 `extension.insert_slice`、转置和分核优化减少离散访存与 padding 开销。"
msgstr "[`tutorial/best_practice/003-fused-cat-slice-conv1d.zh.md`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/003-fused-cat-slice-conv1d.zh.md): Demonstrates how to use `extension.insert_slice`, transpose, and kernel splitting optimization to reduce discrete memory access and padding overhead when fusing cat, slice, and conv1d update."

msgid "复杂 CV 融合建议按数据流分层组织："
msgstr "Complex CV fusion is recommended to be organized hierarchically by data flow."

msgid "**主计算层**：识别哪些步骤必须走 Cube，例如 QK、PV、GEMM、batched matmul。"
msgstr "**Main Compute Layer**: Identifies which steps must go through Cube, such as QK, PV, GEMM, batched matmul."

msgid "**Vector 后处理层**：识别 softmax、activation、mask、scale、normalization、cat/slice、layout transform 等是否能在同一 tile 内完成。"
msgstr "**Vector Post-Processing Layer**: Identifies whether softmax, activation, mask, scale, normalization, cat/slice, layout transform, etc., can be completed within the same tile."

msgid "**访存重排层**：对离散 KV cache、MoE token 重排、短尾轴 tensor，优先在 UB 中用 `extension.insert_slice`、`extension.extract_slice`、转置或借轴转置形成硬件友好的连续访问。"
msgstr "**Memory Access Reordering Layer**: For discrete KV cache, MoE token reordering, and short-tail axis tensors, prioritize using `extension.insert_slice`, `extension.extract_slice`, transpose, or axis-borrowing transpose in UB to form hardware-friendly contiguous access."

msgid "**流水和同步层**：通过 `multibuffer`、`set_workspace_multibuffer`、`tile_mix_vector_loop`、`tile_mix_cube_loop` 等编译选项探索 Cube 与 Vector 的重叠执行。"
msgstr "**Pipeline and Synchronization Layer**: Explore the overlapping execution of Cube and Vector through compilation options such as `multibuffer`, `set_workspace_multibuffer`, `tile_mix_vector_loop`, and `tile_mix_cube_loop`."

msgid "**分核层**：CV 融合算子通常按 Cube Core 数量发射 grid；运行时会以约 1:2 的比例协同 Vector Core。不要简单沿用 GPU 上的大 grid。"
msgstr "**Kernel Splitting**: CV fusion operators typically launch grids based on the number of Cube Cores; the runtime coordinates Vector Cores at a ratio of approximately 1:2. Do not simply adopt the large grid approach used on GPUs."

msgid "对于 attention 类 CV 融合，推荐先让非 causal、短序列、小 head_dim 的 case 跑通，再逐步加入："
msgstr "For attention-based CV fusion, it is recommended to first get non-causal, short-sequence, small head_dim cases running, then gradually add:"

msgid "causal mask 分阶段处理。"
msgstr "The causal mask is processed in stages."

msgid "长序列 K/V block 循环。"
msgstr "Long sequence K/V block loop."

msgid "`m_i`/`l_i` 的数值稳定 softmax 更新。"
msgstr "Numerically stable softmax update for `m_i`/`l_i`."

msgid "HEAD_DIM 较大时的 accumulator workspace 和子块切分。"
msgstr "Accumulator workspace and sub-block partitioning when HEAD_DIM is large."

msgid "KV cache 离散索引下的 load 重排。"
msgstr "Load reordering under KV cache discrete indexing."

msgid "复杂 CV 融合调优时，优先观察 profiling 中 Cube、Vector、MTE2 的时间占比。如果 Cube 等待 Vector，考虑减少 Vector 后处理粒度或打开 CV balance 相关选项；如果 Vector 等待搬运，优先检查离散访存、tail-axis padding 和 multibuffer 配置。"
msgstr "When tuning complex CV fusion, prioritize observing the time proportions of Cube, Vector, and MTE2 in profiling. If Cube is waiting for Vector, consider reducing the granularity of Vector post-processing or enabling CV balance-related options; if Vector is waiting for data movement, first check discrete memory access, tail-axis padding, and multibuffer configuration."

msgid "Triton算子开发指南"
msgstr "Triton Operator Development Guide"

msgid "概述：本文着重介绍了在NPU上进行Triton算子开发中值得注意的问题，分为三个方面：多核任务并行、单核数据搬运、单核数据运算。首先在多核任务并行中介绍了设置最大硬件核数的依据以及具体的实现。然后在单核数据搬运中具体描述了如何设置合适的循环内数据分块大小，并且介绍了过程中常用的优化手段，还补充了可能面临的UB OVERFLOW问题的处理方式。最后回归单个算子，在单核数据运算层面着重介绍了如何开发Triton算子，并强调了相关的关键点。"
msgstr "Overview: This article focuses on notable issues in developing Triton operators on NPU, covering three aspects: multi-core task parallelism, single-core data movement, and single-core data computation. First, in multi-core task parallelism, the basis for setting the maximum number of hardware cores and the specific implementation are introduced. Then, in single-core data movement, it details how to set appropriate data block sizes within loops, describes commonly used optimization techniques, and supplements the handling of potential UB OVERFLOW issues. Finally, returning to individual operators, it emphasizes how to develop Triton operators at the single-core data computation level and highlights relevant key points."

msgid "本指南将通用开发原则和按硬件执行单元划分的算子开发路径分开组织："
msgstr "This guide separates general development principles from operator development paths organized by hardware execution units."

msgid "本页介绍所有 Triton-Ascend 算子都需要关注的通用问题，包括分核、片上内存、访存、Tiling 和 Autotune。"
msgstr "This page introduces common issues that all Triton-Ascend operators need to focus on, including kernel splitting, on-chip memory, memory access, Tiling, and Autotune."

msgid "[Vector 算子开发](./vector_operator.md) 介绍主要由 Vector Core 执行的逐元素、归约、Gather/Scatter 等算子。"
msgstr "[Vector Operator Development](./vector_operator.md) introduces operators such as element-wise, reduction, Gather/Scatter, etc., primarily executed by the Vector Core."

msgid "[Cube 算子开发](./cube_operator.md) 介绍以 `tl.dot`、矩阵乘、批量矩阵乘为核心的算子。"
msgstr "[Cube Operator Development](./cube_operator.md) introduces operators centered around `tl.dot`, matrix multiplication, and batch matrix multiplication."

msgid "[CV 融合算子开发](./cv_fusion_operator.md) 介绍同一个算子中同时存在 Cube 计算和 Vector 后处理、归约、Softmax 或跨核协同的场景。"
msgstr "[CV Fusion Operator Development](./cv_fusion_operator.md) introduces scenarios where Cube computation and Vector post-processing, reduction, Softmax, or cross-core collaboration coexist within the same operator."

msgid "简单算子优先参考本仓 `docs/zh/examples/` 和 `third_party/ascend/tutorials/`；复杂算子优先参考 GitHub 上的 [Ascend/triton-ascend-ops](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops) 中 `tutorial/best_practice/` 的完整优化案例。"
msgstr "For simple operators, refer to `docs/zh/examples/` and `third_party/ascend/tutorials/` in this repository first; for complex operators, refer to the complete optimization cases in `tutorial/best_practice/` from [Ascend/triton-ascend-ops](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops) on GitHub."

msgid "通用多核任务并行"
msgstr "General Multi-core Task Parallelism"

msgid "设置最大硬件核数"
msgstr "Set maximum hardware core count"

msgid "在一个Triton算子中，通常使用grid进行分核操作。对于GPU而言，其计算核心SM通常是几十到几百量级。但是对于昇腾 NPU 平台而言，其计算核心AI Core的数量在几十个的量级。 虽然运行时接口允许下发并发任务数最大为65535，但超过物理核数的部分是通过新一轮的下发来完成的。如果直接将GPU上的Triton算子拿到昇腾平台上运行，这些大量的任务会引入可观的核启动和核初始化时的额外开销，影响到算子性能表现。 因此，需要针对昇腾平台特性修改分核逻辑。最推荐的做法是**将分核的数量直接固定为硬件的物理核数**，在核内做更为细致的数据分块："
msgstr "In a Triton operator, grid-based kernel partitioning is commonly used. For GPUs, the number of compute cores (SMs) is typically on the order of tens to hundreds. However, for the Ascend NPU platform, the number of compute cores (AI Cores) is on the order of tens. Although the runtime interface allows a maximum of 65,535 concurrent tasks to be dispatched, tasks exceeding the number of physical cores are completed through a new round of dispatching. If Triton operators designed for GPUs are directly executed on the Ascend platform, the large number of tasks will introduce significant additional overhead from kernel launching and initialization, negatively impacting operator performance. Therefore, the kernel partitioning logic must be modified to suit the characteristics of the Ascend platform. The most recommended approach is to **fix the number of kernel partitions to the physical core count of the hardware** and perform more fine-grained data partitioning within each core."

msgid "对于纯Vector算子，分核数等于**Vector核数量**"
msgstr "For pure Vector operators, the number of sub-cores equals the **number of Vector cores**."

msgid "对于CV融合算子，分核数等于**Cube核数量**（通常为Vector核数量的一半），算子执行时会按1：2的比例调用Vector核"
msgstr "For the CV fusion operator, the number of sub-cores equals the **number of Cube cores** (typically half the number of Vector cores). When the operator is executed, Vector cores are invoked in a 1:2 ratio."

msgid "一般而言，在NPU卡上，一个计算核心AI Core含有一个cube核，每个cube核配有两个vector核，因此可以通过以下接口获取**Vector核数(vectorcore_num)**与**Cube核数量(aicore_num)**："
msgstr "Generally, on an NPU card, a computing core AI Core contains one cube core, and each cube core is equipped with two vector cores. Therefore, the number of **vector cores (vectorcore_num)** and the number of **cube cores (aicore_num)** can be obtained through the following interfaces:"

msgid "参考示例代码，先固定核数，再通过内部循环分批处理任务分块："
msgstr "Refer to the example code, first fix the number of cores, then process task blocks in batches through an inner loop:"

msgid "通用单核数据搬运"
msgstr "General single-core data transfer"

msgid "设置合适的循环内数据分块大小（BLOCK SIZE）"
msgstr "Set an appropriate BLOCK SIZE for data partitioning within the loop."

msgid "以add_kernel为例，变量和操作共同决定了片上内存空间的占用大，通过修改BLOCK_SIZE大小可以调整循环内数据分块和计算中间结果占用的大小。如果超过上限则算子编译时会提示预期占用大小并报错。要达到最大计算访存比，BLOCK_SIZE需要在不超出片上空间时尽可能大，这可以通过Triton-Ascend的[Autotune](../examples/06_autotune_example.md)预先设置不同的BLOCK_SIZE，运行时会自动选取最优设置。"
msgstr "Taking `add_kernel` as an example, variables and operations together determine the on-chip memory space usage. By modifying the `BLOCK_SIZE`, the size of data blocks within the loop and the intermediate results can be adjusted. If the usage exceeds the upper limit, the operator will prompt the expected usage size and report an error during compilation. To achieve the maximum compute-to-memory ratio, `BLOCK_SIZE` should be as large as possible without exceeding the on-chip space. This can be achieved by using Triton-Ascend's [Autotune](../examples/06_autotune_example.md) to preset different `BLOCK_SIZE` values, and the optimal setting will be automatically selected at runtime."

msgid "尽量保证Tensor的尾轴大小数据对齐"
msgstr "Ensure that the tail axis size data of the Tensor is aligned as much as possible."

msgid "【描述】对于VV类算子需要调用Vector核计算时，昇腾硬件的UB要求Tensor的尾轴大小能被32Bytes整除，而对于CV类算子需要调用vector核和Cube核计算时，要求Tensor的尾轴大小能被512Bytes整除，若尾轴长度不足则会自动补齐。在此前提下，对模型中shape为(2048,3)和(2048,1)Tensor的种种操作，都会因为自动补齐导致性能明显恶化，此时可考虑通过转置操作将对齐轴转到低维，直到store时再转置为原始状态，从而规避自动补齐，优化计算速度。同时由于转置操作本身也受自动补齐规则的影响，因此同样需要特殊技巧来规避补齐。这里列出一个\"借轴转置\"的tip，适用于**tensor.numel() % 256Byte == 0**的场景，具体操作如下："
msgstr "[Description] When VV-type operators need to invoke Vector core computation, the UB of Ascend hardware requires that the size of the last axis of the Tensor be divisible by 32 Bytes. For CV-type operators that require both Vector core and Cube core computation, the size of the last axis must be divisible by 512 Bytes. If the length of the last axis is insufficient, it will be automatically padded. Under this premise, various operations on Tensors with shapes (2048,3) and (2048,1) in the model will experience significant performance degradation due to automatic padding. In such cases, consider using transpose operations to move the alignment axis to a lower dimension, and then transpose back to the original state only when storing, thereby avoiding automatic padding and optimizing computation speed. Additionally, since the transpose operation itself is also affected by the automatic padding rules, special techniques are required to avoid padding. Here is a tip called \"borrow-axis transpose,\" applicable to scenarios where **tensor.numel() % 256Byte == 0**. The specific operation is as follows:"

msgid "注：VV类算子表示该类算子在运算过程中只使用了Vector Core；CV类算子表示该类算子运算过程中既使用了AI Core又使用了Vector Core。"
msgstr "Note: VV-type operators indicate that such operators only use Vector Core during computation; CV-type operators indicate that such operators use both AI Core and Vector Core during computation."

msgid "先将数据搬运到UB上，再从UB中select目标值"
msgstr "First, move the data to UB, then select the target value from UB."

msgid "【描述】在NPU的离散场景下，可以先将数据搬运到UB，再从share中select目标值。"
msgstr "[Description] In the discrete scenario of NPU, data can first be moved to UB, and then the target value can be selected from the share."

msgid "优化前后性能分析和对比"
msgstr "Performance analysis and comparison before and after optimization"

msgid "通过msprof工具执行用例可得到PROF_*文件夹，里面包含了op_summary_\\*.csv文件，该文件可以帮助分析流水情况。注：“\\*”表示时间戳，[性能数据采集参考方法](../debug_guide/profiling.md)。"
msgstr "Using the msprof tool to execute the test case generates a PROF_* folder, which contains the op_summary_*.csv file. This file helps analyze pipeline conditions. Note: \"*\" indicates a timestamp. [Reference method for performance data collection](../debug_guide/profiling.md)."

msgid "Op Name"
msgstr "Op Name"

msgid "aiv_mte2_time(us)"
msgstr "aiv_mte2_time(us)"

msgid "aiv_mte2_ratio"
msgstr "aiv_mte2_ratio"

msgid "未优化"
msgstr "Not optimized"

msgid "pick_kernel"
msgstr "pick_kernel"

msgid "0.686"
msgstr "0.686"

msgid "0.008"
msgstr "0.008"

msgid "优化"
msgstr "Optimization"

msgid "1.041"
msgstr "1.041"

msgid "0.066"
msgstr "0.066"

msgid "通过分析表格中的数据可以发现，优化前后的aiv_mte2_time(us)和aiv_mte2_ratio差距较大，优化方案通过先将大部分数据搬运到UB上，减少小批量数据通过L2搬运到UB的次数，减少了L2搬运到UB上的总时间。"
msgstr "By analyzing the data in the table, it can be observed that there is a significant difference in aiv_mte2_time(us) and aiv_mte2_ratio before and after optimization. The optimization scheme first moves most of the data to UB, reducing the number of times small batches of data are transferred to UB via L2, thereby decreasing the total time for L2-to-UB transfers."

msgid "存算并行"
msgstr "Storage-computation parallelism"

msgid "Triton-Ascend支持两种数据处理模式：存算串行和存算并行。"
msgstr "Triton-Ascend supports two data processing modes: storage-compute serial and storage-compute parallel."

msgid "存算串行：先从全局内存搬运数据到片上内存，完成计算后，再搬运下一批数据。这种方式存在明显的空闲等待时间，效率较低。"
msgstr "Memory-compute serialization: Data is first transferred from global memory to on-chip memory, and after computation is completed, the next batch of data is transferred. This approach has significant idle waiting time and low efficiency."

msgid "存算并行：在搬运第一批数据至片上内存的同时，已开始对其执行计算；随后继续搬运第二批数据，形成“搬运+计算”重叠的流水线式操作，显著提升整体吞吐率。"
msgstr "Storage-computation parallelism: While transferring the first batch of data to on-chip memory, computation on it has already begun; subsequently, the second batch of data is transferred, forming a pipelined operation where \"transfer + computation\" overlap, significantly improving overall throughput."

msgid "实现存算并行的关键在于合理设计数据切分（Tiling）策略，使得在当前批次数据计算过程中，能够提前准备下一阶段所需的数据，从而实现数据搬运与计算过程的并 行化。目前，编译器默认配置multiBuffer=True，默认支持存算并行。"
msgstr "The key to achieving parallel storage and computation lies in properly designing the data tiling strategy, so that during the computation of the current batch of data, the data required for the next stage can be prepared in advance, thereby enabling parallelism between data movement and computation. Currently, the compiler defaults to configuring multiBuffer=True, which supports parallel storage and computation by default."

msgid "Tiling优化"
msgstr "Tiling optimization"

msgid "AI Core进行计算的时候要先将数据搬运至片上内存，而片上内存的空间通常远小于AI Core要处理的总数据量，以Atlas 800T/I A2产品为例，片上内存容量为192KB，默认开启doublebuffer特性后容量还会减至原来的一半。因此算子计算时需要对数据进行分块操作，每次只加载处理其中的一小部分数据。"
msgstr "When AI Core performs computations, data must first be moved to on-chip memory, and the space of on-chip memory is usually much smaller than the total amount of data to be processed by the AI Core. Taking the Atlas 800T/I A2 product as an example, the on-chip memory capacity is 192KB, and after enabling the double buffer feature by default, the capacity is further reduced to half of the original. Therefore, during operator computation, data needs to be partitioned into blocks, with only a small portion of data loaded and processed at a time."

msgid "Triton Autotune 自动调优"
msgstr "Triton Autotune"

msgid "在 Tiling 分块优化中，BLOCK_SIZE、BLOCK_SIZE_SUB等分块参数的取值直接影响算子性能，但手动调试参数组合效率低且难以找到最优值。triton.autotune是Triton框架提供的自动调优工具，能遍历预设的参数配置，通过实际运行对比性能，自动选择最优参数组合，是Tiling优化的核心配套手段。"
msgstr "In Tiling optimization, the values of block parameters such as BLOCK_SIZE and BLOCK_SIZE_SUB directly affect operator performance, but manually tuning parameter combinations is inefficient and makes it difficult to find the optimal values. triton.autotune is an automatic tuning tool provided by the Triton framework that can iterate over preset parameter configurations, compare performance through actual execution, and automatically select the optimal parameter combination, serving as a core supporting method for Tiling optimization."

msgid "如果你关注 Triton-Ascend 上 `configs=[]` 的推荐用法、自动 Tiling 的适用边界，可进一步参考 [Triton-Ascend autotune 使用指南](../autotune_guide.md)。"
msgstr "If you are interested in the recommended usage of `configs=[]` on Triton-Ascend and the applicable boundaries of automatic Tiling, you can further refer to the [Triton-Ascend autotune usage guide](../autotune_guide.md)."

msgid "核心作用 自动遍历参数空间：针对BLOCK_SIZE、BLOCK_SIZE_SUB等 constexpr 类型的分块参数，批量测试不同取值的性能。 性能基准对比：以算子的执行耗时为指标，筛选出适配当前硬件的最优参数。 缓存调优结果：调优后的最优配置会被缓存，后续调用算子时直接复用，避免重复调优。"
msgstr "Core functions: Automatically traverse the parameter space: For constexpr type block parameters such as BLOCK_SIZE and BLOCK_SIZE_SUB, batch test the performance of different values. Performance benchmark comparison: Use the operator execution time as the metric to select the optimal parameters adapted to the current hardware. Cache tuning results: The optimal configuration after tuning is cached, and directly reused in subsequent operator calls to avoid repeated tuning."

msgid "简单示例"
msgstr "Simple example"

msgid "注：设置以下环境变量，便可打印出最优参数信息。"
msgstr "Note: Set the following environment variables to print the optimal parameter information."

msgid "进阶：使用 max_autotune 自动调优"
msgstr "Advanced: Using max_autotune for Automatic Tuning"

msgid "对于 Ascend NPU 算子，要想达到最优性能，除BLOCK_SIZE外，还需调优 num_stages、enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance、tile_mix_vector_loop 等多个硬件相关参数。若使用 @triton.autotune 手动枚举所有组合，会导致配置列表爆炸式增长，代码难以维护。"
msgstr "For Ascend NPU operators, to achieve optimal performance, in addition to BLOCK_SIZE, multiple hardware-related parameters such as num_stages, enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance, and tile_mix_vector_loop also need to be tuned. Manually enumerating all combinations using @triton.autotune would lead to an explosive growth of the configuration list, making the code difficult to maintain."

msgid "max_autotune 是专为 Ascend NPU 设计的扩展装饰器（位于 triton.backends.ascend.runtime），允许用户仅提供基础配置，其余调优参数以列表形式传入，装饰器自动生成全部组合的 Config 列表。"
msgstr "max_autotune is an extension decorator specifically designed for Ascend NPU (located in triton.backends.ascend.runtime), which allows users to provide only the basic configuration while passing the remaining tuning parameters as a list. The decorator automatically generates a complete list of combined Configs."

msgid "核心作用 开发者只需提供少量基础配置（如BLOCK_SIZE），所有与该算子类型相关的编译器选项（例如 num_stages、enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance、tile_mix_vector_loop、enable_ubuf_saving 等）都会通过内置的合理默认值自动纳入最优组合的搜索范围，无需开发者显式列举，一次性完成最优 tiling 和编译器选项组合的自动寻优。若开发者希望对某些参数进行限定，也可通过显式传入列表来覆盖默认搜索范围。"
msgstr "The core function is that developers only need to provide a small amount of basic configuration (such as BLOCK_SIZE), and all compiler options related to this operator type (e.g., num_stages, enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance, tile_mix_vector_loop, enable_ubuf_saving, etc.) will be automatically included in the search range for the optimal combination through built-in reasonable default values, without requiring developers to explicitly enumerate them. This enables one-time automatic optimization for the best tiling and compiler option combination. If developers wish to restrict certain parameters, they can also override the default search range by explicitly passing in a list."

msgid "如何在NPU上避免UB OVERFLOW"
msgstr "How to avoid UB OVERFLOW on NPU"

msgid "【描述】在NPU上，UB或者L1 Size存在上限，当出现该错误时，需要减少单次搬运的数据量，以for循环的方式处理长序列场景。"
msgstr "[Description] On the NPU, there is an upper limit for UB or L1 Size. When this error occurs, it is necessary to reduce the amount of data transferred in a single operation and handle long sequence scenarios in a for-loop manner."

msgid "【注意】A2系列产品UB大小为192KB(1572864 bits)。"
msgstr "[Note] The UB size of A2 series products is 192KB (1572864 bits)."

msgid "通用单核数据运算"
msgstr "General Single-Core Data Computation"

msgid "开发目标"
msgstr "Development objectives"

msgid "在昇腾NPU单核上实现基础数据运算算子（如加减乘除、激活函数、简单矩阵元素运算）。保证算子在单核内高效执行，为后续多核并行和分布式扩展打下基础。"
msgstr "Implement basic data operation operators (such as addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, activation functions, and simple matrix element operations) on a single Ascend NPU core. Ensure efficient execution of the operator within a single core, laying the foundation for subsequent multi-core parallelism and distributed scaling."

msgid "开发步骤"
msgstr "Development Steps"

msgid "1.确定算子功能 -明确输入/输出张量的形状、数据类型（float16/float32/int32 等）。 -确认是否需要广播、边界处理。"
msgstr ""
"1. Determine operator functionality  \n"
"   - Clarify the shape and data type (float16/float32/int32, etc.) of input/output tensors.  \n"
"   - Confirm whether broadcasting or boundary handling is required.\n"

msgid "2.编写核函数（kernel） 单核运算通常对应块级的数据处理。 单核数据运算示例：向量加法"
msgstr "2. Writing the kernel function. Single-kernel operations typically correspond to block-level data processing. Example of single-kernel data operation: vector addition"

msgid "调用："
msgstr "Call:"

msgid "使用上述函数计算两个 torch.tensor 对象的 element-wise sum，并测试其正确性"
msgstr "Use the above function to compute the element-wise sum of two torch.tensor objects and test its correctness."

msgid "3.单核运算的关键点"
msgstr "3. Key Points of Single-Core Computing"

msgid "-块级数据处理：每个计算块负责一小段数据，保证并行性。"
msgstr "Block-level data processing: Each computing block is responsible for a small segment of data, ensuring parallelism."

msgid "-边界检查：使用 mask 或 if (tid < N) 避免越界。"
msgstr "- Boundary check: Use mask or if (tid < N) to avoid out-of-bounds access."

msgid "-块大小选择：合理设置 block 和 grid"
msgstr "Block size selection: properly configure block and grid"

msgid "4.性能要点： (1)访存优化 -保证连续访问。 -使用对齐的 stride，避免跨行/跨列跳跃式访问。 -尽量让数据块大小对齐到 32 字节边界。 输入输出 buffer 在分配时保证对齐，避免访存性能下降。 例:"
msgstr "4. Performance Key Points: (1) Memory Access Optimization - Ensure sequential access. - Use aligned strides to avoid row/column-crossing jumps. - Align data block sizes to 32-byte boundaries as much as possible. Ensure input and output buffers are aligned during allocation to prevent memory access performance degradation. Example:"

msgid "(2)子块划分 -将大矩阵分解为小block，每个block在 UB 内完成计算。 -子块划分要兼顾访存连续性和计算单元利用率。 例："
msgstr "(2) Sub-block partitioning - Decompose the large matrix into small blocks, with each block completing computation within the UB. - Sub-block partitioning must balance memory access continuity and compute unit utilization. Example:"

msgid "通用多维张量切分"
msgstr "General Multidimensional Tensor Slicing"

msgid "Triton 算子处理多维张量时，核心思想是将高维数据映射到硬件的 Block、Core、硬件单元中。本节提供二维与三维张量的典型处理示例。"
msgstr "When Triton operators process multi-dimensional tensors, the core idea is to map high-dimensional data to hardware blocks, cores, and hardware units. This section provides typical processing examples for two-dimensional and three-dimensional tensors."

msgid "二维张量切分：以矩阵乘法（GEMM）为例"
msgstr "2D Tensor Partitioning: Using Matrix Multiplication (GEMM) as an Example"

msgid "对于二维矩阵乘法，通常需要在高度（M）和宽度（N）上进行二维切分，并在深度（K）上进行循环迭代。"
msgstr "For two-dimensional matrix multiplication, it is typically necessary to perform two-dimensional partitioning along the height (M) and width (N), and iterate in a loop along the depth (K)."

msgid "**要点**："
msgstr "**Key Points**:"

msgid "`pid_m` / `pid_n` 分别对应 M / N 维度上的 block 编号"
msgstr "`pid_m` / `pid_n` correspond to the block indices on the M / N dimensions, respectively."

msgid "`stride_*` 显式处理多维步长，避免假设连续内存"
msgstr "`stride_*` explicitly handles multi-dimensional strides to avoid assuming contiguous memory."

msgid "K 维度通过循环分块累加"
msgstr "The K dimension is accumulated through loop tiling."

msgid "三维及以上张量切分：以 Batched GEMM 为例"
msgstr "Slicing of tensors with three or more dimensions: Taking Batched GEMM as an example"

msgid "处理三维张量（如 `[Batch, M, N]`）时，可以将 `Batch` 维度（B）直接映射到 Triton 的 `Grid` 维度上，或者将其与 `M/N` 维度展平后重新映射。"
msgstr "When processing a three-dimensional tensor (e.g., `[Batch, M, N]`), the `Batch` dimension (B) can be directly mapped to Triton's `Grid` dimension, or flattened with the `M/N` dimension and then remapped."

msgid "启动 `Grid` 时增加 `Batch` 维度"
msgstr "Add the `Batch` dimension when starting `Grid`."

msgid "核函数实现"
msgstr "Kernel function implementation"

msgid "`tl.program_id(2)` 取得 Batch 维度的索引"
msgstr "`tl.program_id(2)` gets the index of the Batch dimension."

msgid "每个 Batch 独立计算自己的 `a_batch_ptr` / `b_batch_ptr` / `c_batch_ptr`"
msgstr "Each Batch independently computes its own `a_batch_ptr` / `b_batch_ptr` / `c_batch_ptr`."

msgid "后续 M / N / K 维度的切分逻辑与二维 GEMM 一致"
msgstr "The subsequent splitting logic for the M/N/K dimensions is consistent with that of 2D GEMM."

msgid "Vector 算子开发"
msgstr "Vector Operator Development"

msgid "Vector 算子主要由 Vector Core 执行，典型形态包括逐元素计算、行级归约、类型转换、Gather/Scatter、Mask 更新以及不含 `tl.dot` 的小型融合算子。开发重点不是把 grid 切得越细越好，而是在固定物理 Vector Core 数量的前提下，让每个 program 在核内循环处理多个 tile。"
msgstr "Vector operators are primarily executed by the Vector Core, with typical forms including element-wise computation, row-level reduction, type conversion, Gather/Scatter, Mask update, and small fused operators that do not contain `tl.dot`. The development focus is not on making the grid as fine as possible, but rather on having each program process multiple tiles in a loop within the core, given a fixed number of physical Vector Cores."

msgid "Vector 简单算子开发"
msgstr "Vector Simple Operator Development"

msgid "简单 Vector 算子可以从本仓的 [向量相加样例](../examples/01_vector_add_example.md) 或 `third_party/ascend/tutorials/01-vector-add.py` 入手。该类算子的基本步骤如下："
msgstr "Simple Vector operators can start from the [vector addition example](../examples/01_vector_add_example.md) in this repository or `third_party/ascend/tutorials/01-vector-add.py`. The basic steps for this type of operator are as follows:"

msgid "用 `tl.arange` 构造当前 tile 的连续偏移。"
msgstr "Construct the continuous offset of the current tile using `tl.arange`."

msgid "用 `mask` 保护尾块，避免越界 load/store。"
msgstr "Protect the tail block with `mask` to prevent out-of-bounds load/store."

msgid "完成逐元素计算后写回结果。"
msgstr "Write back the result after completing the element-wise computation."

msgid "当 grid 数远大于物理核数时，将 grid 固定为 `num_vectorcore`，在 kernel 内用 `range(pid, num_blocks, num_core)` 分批处理。"
msgstr "When the number of grids is much larger than the number of physical cores, fix the grid to `num_vectorcore` and process in batches within the kernel using `range(pid, num_blocks, num_core)`."

msgid "基础 kernel 结构如下："
msgstr "The basic kernel structure is as follows:"

msgid "开发时优先检查三类问题："
msgstr "When developing, prioritize checking three types of issues:"

msgid "**数据类型**：Ascend Vector 单元对不同整数类型的支持和性能不同。对于不影响精度的索引、长度、偏移类数据，优先使用 `int32`，可参考 `triton-ascend-ops/tutorial/basic/001-vector_add.zh.md` 和 `002-vector_cmp.zh.md`。"
msgstr "**Data Types**: Ascend Vector units have varying support and performance for different integer types. For index, length, and offset data that do not affect precision, `int32` should be prioritized. Refer to `triton-ascend-ops/tutorial/basic/001-vector_add.zh.md` and `002-vector_cmp.zh.md`."

msgid "**BLOCK_SIZE**：BLOCK_SIZE 需要在 UB 容量内尽量大。若出现 UB overflow，先降低单次处理元素数，再考虑拆分子块。"
msgstr "**BLOCK_SIZE**: BLOCK_SIZE should be as large as possible within the UB capacity. If UB overflow occurs, first reduce the number of elements processed per iteration, then consider splitting into sub-blocks."

msgid "**分核数**：NPU 物理 Vector Core 数量通常为几十个。小 tile 大 grid 的 GPU 写法迁移到 NPU 时，容易因多轮下发带来明显开销。"
msgstr "**Number of Cores**: The number of NPU physical Vector Cores is typically several dozen. When migrating GPU code written with small tiles and large grids to NPU, it is prone to significant overhead due to multiple dispatch rounds."

msgid "Vector 复杂算子开发"
msgstr "Vector Complex Operator Development"

msgid "复杂 Vector 算子通常不是单个逐元素表达式，而是带有离散访存、批量重排、多个输出或长 hidden size 的组合逻辑。可参考 [Ascend/triton-ascend-ops](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops) 中的以下案例："
msgstr "Complex Vector operators are typically not single element-wise expressions, but rather combined logic involving discrete memory access, batch rearrangement, multiple outputs, or long hidden sizes. Refer to the following examples in [Ascend/triton-ascend-ops](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops):"

msgid "[`tutorial/best_practice/004-gather_scatter.py`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/004-gather_scatter.py)：Megablocks gather/scatter/scatter_wgrad 的 Ascend 亲和实现。"
msgstr "[`tutorial/best_practice/004-gather_scatter.py`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/004-gather_scatter.py): Ascend-friendly implementation of Megablocks gather/scatter/scatter_wgrad."

msgid "[`tutorial/best_practice/005-binned_gather_scatter.py`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/005-binned_gather_scatter.py)：按 expert/bin 分组后的 gather/scatter。"
msgstr "[`tutorial/best_practice/005-binned_gather_scatter.py`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/005-binned_gather_scatter.py): gather/scatter after grouping by expert/bin."

msgid "[`tutorial/best_practice/006-padded_gather_scatter.py`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/006-padded_gather_scatter.py)：带 padding 的 MoE gather/scatter。"
msgstr "[`tutorial/best_practice/006-padded_gather_scatter.py`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/006-padded_gather_scatter.py): MoE gather/scatter with padding."

msgid "这类算子的组织方式通常是："
msgstr "The organization of this type of operator is usually:"

msgid "**按物理核切分外层任务**：用 `num_vectorcore` 作为 grid，每个 program 负责一段 indices 或 token。"
msgstr "**Partition outer tasks by physical cores**: Use `num_vectorcore` as the grid, with each program responsible for a segment of indices or tokens."

msgid "**按 UB 容量切分 hidden 维**：对 `NUM_COLUMNS` 使用 `BLOCK_X` 分块，并预留 double buffer、索引和临时张量的空间。"
msgstr "**Split hidden dimension by UB capacity**: Use `BLOCK_X` to partition `NUM_COLUMNS`, and reserve space for double buffer, indices, and temporary tensors."

msgid "**用 `SUB_BLOCK_SIZE` 合并小粒度离散任务**：一次加载一组 indices，在 UB 中组织成连续临时块，减少 GM 标量访存和多次 store。"
msgstr "**Merge small-grained discrete tasks with `SUB_BLOCK_SIZE`**: Load a group of indices at once, organize them into contiguous temporary blocks in UB, reducing GM scalar memory access and multiple stores."

msgid "**用扩展语义管理 UB 内局部数据**：先通过 `import triton.language.extra.cann.extension as extension` 引入扩展模块，再使用 `extension.insert_slice` 合并多行数据，使用 `extension.extract_slice` 取出子块后再分散写回。"
msgstr "**Managing Local Data in UB with Extended Semantics**: First, import the extension module using `import triton.language.extra.cann.extension as extension`, then use `extension.insert_slice` to merge multiple rows of data, and use `extension.extract_slice` to extract sub-blocks before scattering them back."

msgid "**为尾块保留统一 mask**：复杂 gather/scatter 中同时存在 index mask、column mask 和 expert/bin 边界，建议分别命名并只在 load/store 处组合。"
msgstr "**Reserve a unified mask for the tail block**: In complex gather/scatter operations, index mask, column mask, and expert/bin boundaries coexist. It is recommended to name them separately and combine them only at load/store points."

msgid "典型的 UB 预算思路如下："
msgstr "A typical UB budgeting approach is as follows:"

msgid "当复杂 Vector 算子性能不达预期时，优先从以下方向排查："
msgstr "When the performance of a complex Vector operator does not meet expectations, prioritize troubleshooting from the following directions:"

msgid "grid 是否远大于物理 Vector Core 数，导致多轮下发。"
msgstr "Whether the grid is much larger than the number of physical Vector Cores, causing multiple rounds of distribution."

msgid "离散访存是否可转化为“批量搬入 UB 后在 UB 内选择”。"
msgstr "Whether discrete memory access can be transformed into \"batch loading into UB followed by selection within UB\"."

msgid "尾轴是否满足 32B 对齐；不满足时是否可用转置或借轴转置规避自动 padding。"
msgstr "Whether the tail axis satisfies 32B alignment; if not, whether transposition or borrowing axis transposition can be used to avoid automatic padding."

msgid "`BLOCK_X` 和 `SUB_BLOCK_SIZE` 是否造成 UB overflow 或过小的搬运粒度。"
msgstr "Whether `BLOCK_X` and `SUB_BLOCK_SIZE` cause UB overflow or excessively small transfer granularity."

