msgstr "`device_print` is used to print information from the device side during NPU runtime. Unlike `static_print`, it outputs information in real-time during kernel execution. The first parameter must be a `string`, and subsequent parameters must be `scalars` or `tensors`. **To use `device_print`, set the environment variable `TRITON_DEVICE_PRINT` to `True`.**"

