msgid "al.scope 接口文档"
msgstr "al.scope API Documentation"

msgid "昇腾处理器包含多种类型的计算单元（例如，用于矩阵运算的 Cube Unit 和用于向量/标量运算的 Vector Unit）。al.scope 允许内核开发者显式地告诉 Triton 编译器，特定代码区域应该目标哪种硬件单元，从而实现更精细的性能调优和资源利用。"
msgstr "The Ascend processor contains multiple types of computing units (e.g., Cube Unit for matrix operations and Vector Unit for vector/scalar operations). `al.scope` allows kernel developers to explicitly tell the Triton compiler which hardware unit a specific code region should target, enabling finer-grained performance tuning and resource utilization."

msgid "al.scope 是 triton.language.extra.ascend 模块中的一个上下文管理器（Context Manager），专为 Triton 内核中的代码块指定 昇腾硬件的执行模式。"
msgstr "al.scope is a context manager in the triton.language.extra.ascend module, specifically used to specify the execution mode of Ascend hardware for code blocks within Triton kernels."

msgid "常用值说明"
msgstr "Common Values Description"

msgid "each kernel have 1 scope for cube and vector, inside them they run parallely and there are other syncing operations that declares the sync between both of the scope"
msgstr "Each kernel has one scope for cube and vector, inside which they run in parallel, and there are other synchronization operations that declare the sync between both scopes."

msgid "Parallel Execution: Operations within cube and vector scopes execute in parallel"
msgstr "Parallel Execution: Operations within cube and vector scopes execute in parallel."

msgid "Single Scope per Type: Each kernel supports one cube scope and one vector scope (?)"
msgstr "Single Scope per Type: Each kernel supports one cube scope and one vector scope (?)"

msgid "Explicit Synchronization: Required for data dependencies between scopes using sync operations"
msgstr "Explicit Synchronization: Required for data dependencies between scopes using sync operations"

msgid "sub_vec_id"
msgstr "sub_vec_id"

msgid "昇腾硬件AIC与AIV核数配比不同（1:N），Triton编程抽象屏蔽了Cube核与Vector核的硬件细节，因此，Triton算子开发者无法控制如何切分数据在N个Vector核间并行处理，由编译器通过AutoSubTiling Pass自动实现。"
msgstr "The ratio of AIC to AIV cores in Ascend hardware varies (1:N). Triton's programming abstraction hides the hardware details of Cube and Vector cores, so Triton operator developers cannot control how to split data for parallel processing across N Vector cores. This is automatically handled by the compiler through the AutoSubTiling Pass."

msgid "sub_vec_id编程接口返回N个Vector核的sub id，允许算子开发者根据vector核sub id决定每个核处理哪些数据。"
msgstr "The sub_vec_id programming interface returns the sub IDs of N Vector cores, allowing operator developers to decide which data each core processes based on the vector core sub ID."

msgid "返回值：返回范围为 [0, N) 的 Sub Vector ID，算子开发者可根据该ID决定N个并行Vector核中每个核处理的数据分片"
msgstr "Return value: Returns the Sub Vector ID in the range [0, N). The operator developer can use this ID to determine the data slice processed by each of the N parallel Vector cores."

msgid "入参：无"
msgstr "Input parameters: none"

msgid "仅在AIC和AIV核混合使用场景中有效，不可在纯Cube类算子或者纯Vector类算子中使用，否则会触发编译报错。"
msgstr "Only valid in scenarios where AIC and AIV cores are used together; it cannot be used in pure Cube-type operators or pure Vector-type operators, otherwise a compilation error will be triggered."

msgid "subview"
msgstr "subview"

msgid "昇腾硬件 A5 支持了定义新视图，仅通过偏移、大小和步幅实现，不复制底层数据。"
msgstr "Ascend hardware A5 supports defining new views, implemented only through offset, size, and stride, without copying the underlying data."

